{
  "title": "4: al-Nisaa النساء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ وَّخَلَقَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا وَبَثَّ مِنْهُمَا رِجَالًا كَثِيْرًا وَّنِسَآءً ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ تَسَآءَلُوْنَ بِهٖ وَالْاَرْحَامَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيْبًا‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO TAQOO RABBAKOMUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN WWAKHALAQA MINHAA ZAWJAHAA WA BASSA MINHOMAA REJAALAN KASEERAA WWANESAAAN WAT TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE TASAAALOONA BEHI WAL AARHAAMA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAYKUM RAQEEBAN.\nO mankind! reverence your Guardian-Lord, who created you from a single person, created, of like nature, His mate, and from them twain scattered (like seeds) countless men and women;- reverence Allah, through whom ye demand your mutual (rights), and (reverence) the wombs (That bore you): for Allah ever watches over you. \nوَاٰ تُوا الْيَتٰمٰٓى اَمْوَالَهُمْ وَلَا تَتَبَدَّلُوا الْخَبِيْثَ بِالطَّيِّبِ وَلَا تَاْكُلُوْۤا اَمْوَالَهُمْ اِلٰٓى اَمْوَالِكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حُوْبًا كَبِيْرًا‏‏(2)\nWAA TOOA AL-YATAAMAAA AMWAALAHUM WA LAA TATABADDALOOA KHABEESA BEALTTAYBE WA LAA TAAKULOOA AMWAALAHUM ELAA AAMWAALEKUM INNAHU KAANA HOOBAN KABEERAA.\nTo orphans restore their property (When they reach their age), nor substitute (your) worthless things for (their) good ones; and devour not their substance (by mixing it up) with your own. For this is indeed a great sin. \nوَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَلَّا تُقْسِطُوْا فِى الْيَتٰمٰى فَانْكِحُوْا مَا طَابَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ النِّسَآءِ مَثْنٰى وَثُلٰثَ وَرُبٰعَ ۚ فَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَلَّا تَعْدِلُوْا فَوَاحِدَةً اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ اَدْنٰٓى اَلَّا تَعُوْلُوْا ؕ‏(3)\nWA KHIFTUM ALLAA TUQSETOOA FIL AL-YATAAMAA FAANKEHOOA MAA TAABA LAKUM MENAL NESAAA-E MASNAA WASULAASA WARUBAAA’A FA-IN KHIFTUM ALLAA TAA’DELOOA FAWAAHEDATAN AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM ZAA LEKA TAQARRA ALLAA TAU’OOLOOA.\nIf ye fear that ye shall not be able to deal justly with the orphans, Marry women of your choice, Two or three or four; but if ye fear that ye shall not be able to deal justly (with them), then only one, or (a captive) that your right hands possess, that will be more suitable, to prevent you from doing injustice. \nوَاٰ تُوا النِّسَآءَ صَدُقٰتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً ؕ فَاِنْ طِبْنَ لَكُمْ عَنْ شَىْءٍ مِّنْهُ نَفْسًا فَكُلُوْهُ هَنِيْٓئًا مَّرِیْٓٴًﺎ‏(4)\nWAA TOOA NESAAA-A SADUQAATEHENNA NEHLATAN FA-IN TEBNA LAKUM A’N SHAY-IN MINHO NAFSAN FAKULOOHU HANEEAN MMARE.\nAnd give the women (on marriage) their dower as a free gift; but if they, of their own good pleasure, remit any part of it to you, Take it and enjoy it with right good cheer. \nوَلَا تُؤْتُوا السُّفَهَآءَ اَمْوَالَكُمُ الَّتِىْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ قِيٰمًا وَّارْزُقُوْهُمْ فِيْهَا وَاكْسُوْهُمْ وَقُوْلُوْا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوْفًا‏(5)\nWA LAA TUTOOA AS-SUFAHAAA AAMWAALAKUMU LATEE JA-A’LA LAAHO LAKUM QEEMAN WWAARZUQOOHUM FEEHAA WAAKSOOHUM WA QOOLOO LAHUM QAWLAM MA’ROOFAA.\nTo those weak of understanding Make not over your property, which Allah hath made a means of support for you, but feed and clothe them therewith, and speak to them words of kindness and justice. \nوَابْتَلُوا الْيَتٰمٰى حَتّٰىۤ اِذَا بَلَغُوا النِّكَاحَ ۚ فَاِنْ اٰنَسْتُمْ مِّنْهُمْ رُشْدًا فَادْفَعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِمْ اَمْوَالَهُمْۚ وَلَا تَاْكُلُوْهَاۤ اِسْرَافًا وَّبِدَارًا اَنْ يَّكْبَرُوْا ؕ وَمَنْ كَانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ ۚ وَمَنْ كَانَ فَقِيْرًا فَلْيَاْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ ؕ فَاِذَا دَفَعْتُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ اَمْوَالَهُمْ فَاَشْهِدُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ حَسِيْبًا‏(6)\nWAABTALOOA AL-YATAAMAA HATTAA EZAA BALAGHOOA AN-NEKAAHA FA-IN AAANASTUM MINHUM RUSHDAN FAADFAU’OOA ELAYHIM AMWAALAHUM WA LAA TAAKULOOHAA AESRAAFAN WWABEDAARAN AN YYAKBAROOA WA MAN KAANA GHANEEA FALYASTAA’FEF WA MAN KAANA FAQEERAN FALYAAKUL BIL-MA’ROOF FA-EZAA DAFAA’TUM ELAYHIM AMWAALAHUM FAASHHEDOOA A’LAYHIM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE HASEEBAA.\nMake trial of orphans until they reach the age of marriage; if then ye find sound judgment in them, release their property to them; but consume it not wastefully, nor in haste against their growing up. If the guardian is well-off, Let him claim no remuneration, but if he is poor, let him have for himself what is just and reasonable. When ye release their property to them, take witnesses in their presence: But all-sufficient is Allah in taking account. \nلِلرِّجَالِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ مِمَّا قَلَّ مِنْهُ اَوْ كَثُرَ ؕ نَصِيْبًا مَّفْرُوْضًا‏(7)\nLELRREJAALE NASEEBUM MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA WALELNNESAAE NASEEBUM MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA MIMMAA QALLA MINHO AW KASURA NASEEBAN MMAFROOZAN.\nFrom what is left by parents and those nearest related there is a share for men and a share for women, whether the property be small or large, a determinate share. \nوَاِذَا حَضَرَ الْقِسْمَةَ اُولُوا الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنُ فَارْزُقُوْهُمْ مِّنْهُ وَقُوْلُوْا لَهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوْفًا‏(8)\nWA EZAA HAZARA AL-QESMATA ULUL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENU FAARZUQOOHUM MINHO WA QOOLOO LAHUM QAWLAM MA’ROOFAA.\nBut if at the time of division other relatives, or orphans or poor, are present, feed them out of the (property), and speak to them words of kindness and justice. \nوَلْيَخْشَ الَّذِيْنَ لَوْ تَرَكُوْا مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّةً ضِعٰفًا خَافُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ فَلْيَتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَلْيَقُوْلُوا قَوْلًا سَدِيْدًا‏(9)\nWALYAKHSHA LAZEENA LAW TARAKOO MIN KHALFEHIM ZURREETAN ZEA’AAFAN KHAAFOOA A’LAYHIM FALYATTAQOOA LAAHA WALYAQOOLOOA QAWLAM SADEEDAY.\nLet those (disposing of an estate) have the same fear in their minds as they would have for their own if they had left a helpless family behind: Let them fear Allah, and speak words of appropriate (comfort). \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَاْكُلُوْنَ اَمْوَالَ الْيَتٰمٰى ظُلْمًا اِنَّمَا يَاْكُلُوْنَ فِىْ بُطُوْنِهِمْ نَارًا ؕ وَسَيَصْلَوْنَ سَعِيْرًا‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAAKOLOON AAMWAALA AL-YATAAMAA ZULMAWN INNAMAA YAAKOLOON FEE BOTOONEHIM NAARAN WASAYASLAWNA SA-E’ERAA.\nThose who unjustly eat up the property of orphans, eat up a Fire into their own bodies: They will soon be enduring a Blazing Fire! \nيُوْصِيْكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْۤ اَوْلَادِكُمْ لِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ۚ فَاِنْ كُنَّ نِسَآءً فَوْقَ اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُنَّ ثُلُثَا مَا تَرَكَ ۚ وَاِنْ كَانَتْ وَاحِدَةً فَلَهَا النِّصْفُ ؕ وَلِاَ بَوَيْهِ لِكُلِّ وَاحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ مِمَّا تَرَكَ اِنْ كَانَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّوَرِثَهٗۤ اَبَوٰهُ فَلِاُمِّهِ الثُّلُثُ ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَهٗۤ اِخْوَةٌ فَلِاُمِّهِ السُّدُسُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصِىْ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَيْنٍ ؕ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ وَاَبْنَآؤُكُمْ ۚ لَا تَدْرُوْنَ اَيُّهُمْ اَقْرَبُ لَكُمْ نَفْعًا ؕ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(11)\nYOOSEEKUMU LAAHO FEE AAWLAADEKUM LELZZAKARE LAZEE HAZZE AL-AUNSAYAYNE FA-IN KUNNA NESAAAN FAWQA ASNATAYNE FA LAHUNNA SULUSAA MAA TARAKA WA KAANAT WAAHEDATAN FA LAHAA AN-NESFU WALEAA BAWAYHE LEKULLIM WAAHEDIN MINHOMAA WA AS-SUDUSU MIMMAA TARAKA IN KAANA LAHU WALADUN FA-IN LAM YAKUL LAHU WALADUN WWAWARESAH AABAWHU FALEAUMMEHE AS-SULUSU FA-IN KAANA LAHU AEKHWATUN FALEAUMMEHE AS-SUDUSU MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSEAA BEHAA AW DAYNIN AAABAAUKUM WAABNAAUKUM LAA TADROONA AAYHUM AQRABO LAKUM BEKUM FAREEZATANW MENAL LAAHE INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAllah (thus) directs you as regards your Children's (Inheritance): to the male, a portion equal to that of two females: if only daughters, two or more, their share is two-thirds of the inheritance; if only one, her share is a half. For parents, a sixth share of the inheritance to each, if the deceased left children; if no children, and the parents are the (only) heirs, the mother has a third; if the deceased Left brothers (or sisters) the mother has a sixth. (The distribution in all cases ('s) after the payment of legacies and debts. Ye know not whether your parents or your children are nearest to you in benefit. These are settled portions ordained by Allah; and Allah is All-knowing, Al-wise. \nوَلَكُمْ نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ اَزْوَاجُكُمْ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُنَّ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَهُنَّ وَلَدٌ فَلَكُمُ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصِيْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ؕ وَلَهُنَّ الرُّبُعُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّكُمْ وَلَدٌ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ وَلَدٌ فَلَهُنَّ الثُّمُنُ مِمَّا تَرَكْتُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ تُوْصُوْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ رَجُلٌ يُّوْرَثُ كَلٰلَةً اَوِ امْرَاَةٌ وَّلَهٗۤ اَخٌ اَوْ اُخْتٌ فَلِكُلِّ وَاحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا السُّدُسُ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَكْثَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ فَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فِى الثُّلُثِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُّوْصٰى بِهَاۤ اَوْ دَ يْنٍ ۙ غَيْرَ مُضَآرٍّ ۚ وَصِيَّةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَلِيْمٌ ؕ‏(12)\nWA LAKUM NESFU MAA TARAKA AAZWAAJUKUM IN LAM YAKUL LEBAASUL WALADUN FA-IN KAANA LAHUNNA WALADUN FA LAKOMUL AR-RUBUU’U MIMMAA TARAKNA MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSEENA BEHAA AW DA YNIN MISLUL AR-RUBUU’U MIMMAA TARAKTUM IN LAM YAKUL LAKUM WALADUN FA-IN KAANA LAKUM WALADUN FA LAHUNNA AS-SUMUNU MIMMAA TARAKTUM MIN BA’DE WASEETIN TOOSOONA BEHAA AW DA YNIN WA KAANA RAJOLUM YYOORASU KALAALATAN AWE’ AMRAATUN WWALAH AAKHUN AW AUKHTUN FA LEKULLIM WAAHEDIN MINHOMAA WA AS-SUDUSU FA-IN KAANOO AKSARAN MIN ZAA LEKA FAHUM SHURAKAAU FIL AS-SULUSE MIN BA’DE WASEETIN YYOOSAA BEHAA AW DA YNIN GHAYRA MUZAARRIN WASEETAN MENAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HALEEM.\n In what your wives leave, your share is a half, if they leave no child; but if they leave a child, ye get a fourth; after payment of legacies and debts. In what ye leave, their share is a fourth, if ye leave no child; but if ye leave a child, they get an eighth; after payment of legacies and debts. If the man or woman whose inheritance is in question, has left neither ascendants nor descendants, but has left a brother or a sister, each one of the two gets a sixth; but if more than two, they share in a third; after payment of legacies and debts; so that no loss is caused (to any one). Thus is it ordained by Allah; and Allah is All-knowing, Most Forbearing. \nتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ يُدْخِلْهُ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(13)\nTILKA TILKA LAAHE WA MAN YOTE-I’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU YUDKHILHO JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAZAA LEKA FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nThose are limits set by Allah: those who obey Allah and His Messenger will be admitted to Gardens with rivers flowing beneath, to abide therein (for ever) and that will be the supreme achievement. \nوَمَنْ يَّعْصِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُوْدَهٗ يُدْخِلْهُ نَارًا خَالِدًا فِيْهَا وَلَهٗ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(14)\nWA MAN YA’ASIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAYATAA’ADDA HUDOODAH YUDKHILHO NAARAN KHAALEDAN FEEHAA WA LAHU A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nBut those who disobey Allah and His Messenger and transgress His limits will be admitted to a Fire, to abide therein: And they shall have a humiliating punishment. \nوَالّٰتِىْ يَاْتِيْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِكُمْ فَاسْتَشْهِدُوْا عَلَيْهِنَّ اَرْبَعَةً مِّنْكُمْ ۚ فَاِنْ شَهِدُوْا فَاَمْسِكُوْهُنَّ فِى الْبُيُوْتِ حَتّٰى يَتَوَفّٰٮهُنَّ الْمَوْتُ اَوْ يَجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَهُنَّ سَبِيْلًا‏(15)\nWA KHAALEKA YAATEENA FAAHESHATA MIN NESAAA-EKUM FAASTASHHEDOOA A’LAYHINNA ARBA-A’TAM MINKUM FA-IN SHAHEDOOA FA-AMSEKOOHUNNA FIL AL-BUYOOTE HATTAA YATAWAFFAAHUNNA MAWTO AW YAJA’ALA LAAHO LAHUNNA SABEELAA.\nIf any of your women are guilty of lewdness, Take the evidence of four (Reliable) witnesses from amongst you against them; and if they testify, confine them to houses until death do claim them, or Allah ordain for them some (other) way. \nوَالَّذٰنِ يَاْتِيٰنِهَا مِنْكُمْ فَاٰذُوْهُمَا ۚ فَاِنْ تَابَا وَاَصْلَحَا فَاَعْرِضُوْا عَنْهُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ تَوَّابًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(16)\nWAALLAZAANE YAATEENEHAA MINKUM FAAZOOHUMAA FA-IN TAABAA WAASLAHAA FAAA’REZOOA A’ANHUMAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA TAWWAABAA RAHEEMAA.\nIf two men among you are guilty of lewdness, punish them both. If they repent and amend, Leave them alone; for Allah is Oft-returning, Most Merciful. \nاِنَّمَا التَّوْبَةُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السُّوْٓءَ بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ يَتُوْبُوْنَ مِنْ قَرِيْبٍ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَتُوْبُ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(17)\nINNAMAA AT-TAWBATU A’LAL LAAHE LILLAZEENA YA’MALOON AS-SOOA BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA YATOOBOONA MIN QAREEBIN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YATOOBU LAAHO WA KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAllah accept the repentance of those who do evil in ignorance and repent soon afterwards; to them will Allah turn in mercy: For Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom. \nوَلَيْسَتِ التَّوْبَةُ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ۚ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا حَضَرَ اَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ اِنِّىْ تُبْتُ الْئٰنَ وَلَا الَّذِيْنَ يَمُوْتُوْنَ وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا‏(18)\nWA LAYSATIL AT-TAWBATU LILLAZEENA YA’MALOON SAYYE-AATE HATTAA EZAA HAZARA AAHADAHUMU MAWTO QAALA INNEE TUBTU AL-AANA WA LAA LAZEENA YAMOOTOONA WA HUM KUFFAARUN OOLAAA-EKA A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nOf no effect is the repentance of those who continue to do evil, until death faces one of them, and he says, “Now have I repented indeed;” nor of those who die rejecting Faith: for them have We prepared a punishment most grievous. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ اَنْ تَرِثُوا النِّسَآءَ كَرْهًا ؕ وَلَا تَعْضُلُوْهُنَّ لِتَذْهَبُوْا بِبَعْضِ مَاۤ اٰتَيْتُمُوْهُنَّ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّاْتِيْنَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ ۚ وَعَاشِرُوْهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ ۚ فَاِنْ كَرِهْتُمُوْهُنَّ فَعَسٰۤى اَنْ تَكْرَهُوْا شَيْئًا وَّيَجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِ خَيْرًا كَثِيْرًا‏(19)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA YAHILLO LAKUM AN TARESOOA NESAAA-A AW WA LAA TA’ZOLOOHUNNA LETAZHABOOA BE-BA’ZIL MAA MIMMAA ILLAA AN YAKHRUJNA MINKUNNA BE-FAAHESHATIM WAA’AASHEROOHUNNA BIL-MA’ROOF FA-IN KAREHTUMOOHUNNA FA A’SAA AN TAKRAHOO SHAY-ANW WWAYAJA’ALA LAAHO FEEHE KHAYRAN KASEERAA.\nO ye who believe! Ye are forbidden to inherit women against their will. Nor should ye treat them with harshness, that ye may Take away part of the dower ye have given them, except where they have been guilty of open lewdness; on the contrary live with them on a footing of kindness and equity. If ye take a dislike to them it may be that ye dislike a thing, and Allah brings about through it a great deal of good. \nوَاِنْ اَرَدتُّمُ اسْتِبْدَالَ زَوْجٍ مَّكَانَ زَوْجٍ ۙ وَّاٰتَيْتُمْ اِحْدٰٮهُنَّ قِنْطَارًا فَلَا تَاْخُذُوْا مِنْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ اَ تَاْخُذُوْنَهٗ بُهْتَانًا وَّاِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(20)\nWA AARADTTUMU ASTEBDAALA ZAWJIN MMAKAANA ZAWJIN WWAATAYTUM AEHDAAHUNNA QENTAARAN FALAA AN MINHO SHAY-ANW A’ZAABAN TAAKHUZOONAH BOHTAANANW WA ISMAM MOBEENAA.\nBut if ye decide to take one wife in place of another, even if ye had given the latter a whole treasure for dower, Take not the least bit of it back: Would ye take it by slander and manifest wrong? \nوَ كَيْفَ تَاْخُذُوْنَهٗ وَقَدْ اَفْضٰى بَعْضُكُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّاَخَذْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِّيْثَاقًا غَلِيْظًا‏(21)\nWA KAYFA TAAKHUZOONAH WA QAD AAFZAA BA’ZOKUM ELAA ELAA WWAAKHAZNA MINKUM MMEESAAQAN GHALEEZAA.\nAnd how could ye take it when ye have gone in unto each other, and they have Taken from you a solemn covenant? \nوَلَا تَنْكِحُوْا مَا نَكَحَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ مِّنَ النِّسَآءِ اِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً وَّمَقْتًا ؕ وَسَآءَ سَبِيْلًا‏(22)\nWA LAA LAA MAA NAKAHA AAABAAUKUM MENAL NESAAA-E ILLAA MAA QAD SALAFA INNAHU KAANA FAAHESHATAN WWAMAQTAN WA SAAA-A SABEELAA.\nAnd marry not women whom your fathers married, except what is past: It was shameful and odious, an abominable custom indeed. \nحُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ اُمَّهٰتُكُمْ وَبَنٰتُكُمْ وَاَخَوٰتُكُمْ وَعَمّٰتُكُمْ وَخٰلٰتُكُمْ وَبَنٰتُ الْاٰخِ وَبَنٰتُ الْاُخْتِ وَاُمَّهٰتُكُمُ الّٰتِىْۤ اَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَاَخَوٰتُكُمْ مِّنَ الرَّضَاعَةِ وَ اُمَّهٰتُ نِسَآئِكُمْ وَرَبَآئِبُكُمُ الّٰتِىْ فِىْ حُجُوْرِكُمْ مِّنْ نِّسَآئِكُمُ الّٰتِىْ دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَاِنْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَحَلَاۤئِلُ اَبْنَآئِكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ اَصْلَابِكُمْۙ وَاَنْ تَجْمَعُوْا بَيْنَ الْاُخْتَيْنِ اِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا ۙ‏(23)\nHURREMAT A’LAYKUM AUMMAHAATUKUM WABANAATUKUM WAAKHAWTUKUM WAA’AMMAATUKUM WAKHAALAATUKUM WABANAATU AL-AAAKHE WABANAATU AL-AUKHTE WAAMMAHAATUKUMU KHAALEKA AARZAA’NAKUM WAAKHAWTUKUM MENAL AR-RAZAAA’ATE WA AUMMAHAATU NESAAEKUM WARABAAAEBUKUMU KHAALEKA FEE HUJOOREKUM MIN NNESAAEKUMU KHAALEKA DAKHALTUM BEHINNA FA-IN LAM TAKOONOO DAKHALTUM BEHINNA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM WAHALAAELU AABNAAEKUMU LAZEENA MIN AASLAABEKUM WA TAJMAU’OOA BAYNA AL-AUKHTAYNE ILLAA MAA QAD SALAF INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nProhibited to you (For marriage) are:- Your mothers, daughters, sisters; father's sisters, Mother's sisters; brother's daughters, sister's daughters; foster-mothers (Who gave you suck), foster-sisters; your wives' mothers; your step-daughters under your guardianship, born of your wives to whom ye have gone in, no prohibition if ye have not gone in;- (Those who have been) wives of your sons proceeding from your loins; and two sisters in wedlock at one and the same time, except for what is past; for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful;- \nوَّالْمُحْصَنٰتُ مِنَ النِّسَآءِ اِلَّا مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْۚ كِتٰبَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْۚ وَاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ مَّا وَرَآءَ ذٰ لِكُمْ اَنْ تَبْتَغُوْا بِاَمْوَالِكُمْ مُّحْصِنِيْنَ غَيْرَ مُسَافِحِيْنَ ؕ فَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُمْ بِهٖ مِنْهُنَّ فَاٰ تُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ فَرِيْضَةً ؕ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيْمَا تَرٰضَيْتُمْ بِهٖ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الْفَرِيْضَةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(24)\nWWAALMUHSANAATU MENAL NESAAA-E ILLAA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM KETAABAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA OHILLA LAKUM MAA WARAAA-A ZAA ZAALEKUM AN TABTAGHOO BE-ANWAALEKUM MMUHSENEENA GHAYRA MUSAAFEHEENA FAMAA ASTAMTAA’TUM BEHI MINHUNNA FA-AATOOHUNNA OJOORAHUN OJOORAHUNNA FAREEZATANW WA LAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM FEEMAA TARAAZAYTUM BEHI MIN BA’DE AL-FAREEZATE INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\n(5)  Also (prohibited are) women already married, except those whom your right hands possess: Thus hath Allah ordained (Prohibitions) against you: Except for these, all others are lawful, provided ye seek (them in marriage) with gifts from your property, desiring chastity, not lust, seeing that ye derive benefit from them, give them their dowers (at least) as prescribed; but if, after a dower is prescribed, agree Mutually (to vary it), there is no blame on you, and Allah is All-knowing, All-wise. \nوَمَنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ مِنْكُمْ طَوْلًا اَنْ يَّنْكِحَ الْمُحْصَنٰتِ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ فَمِنْ مَّا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ مِّنْ فَتَيٰتِكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِاِيْمَانِكُمْ ؕ بَعْضُكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْضٍ ۚ فَانْكِحُوْهُنَّ بِاِذْنِ اَهْلِهِنَّ وَاٰ تُوْهُنَّ اُجُوْرَهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ مُحْصَنٰتٍ غَيْرَ مُسٰفِحٰتٍ وَّلَا مُتَّخِذٰتِ اَخْدَانٍ ؕ فَاِذَاۤ اُحْصِنَّ فَاِنْ اَ تَيْنَ بِفَاحِشَةٍ فَعَلَيْهِنَّ نِصْفُ مَا عَلَى الْمُحْصَنٰتِ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ خَشِىَ الْعَنَتَ مِنْكُمْ ؕ وَاَنْ تَصْبِرُوْا خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWA MAN LAM YASTATEA’ MINKUM TAWLAN AN YYANKEHA AL-MUHSANAATE MOAMENAATE FAMIN MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM MIN FATAYTEKUMU MOAMENAATE WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BE-EEMAANEKUM BA’ZOKUM MIN ELAA FAANKEHOOHUNNA BE-IZNIL AAHLEHENNA WAA OJOORAHUN OJOORAHUNNA BIL-MA’ROOF MUHSANAATIN GHAYRA MUSAAFEHAATIN WA LAA MUTTAKHEZAATE AAKHDAANIN FA-EZAA AUHSENNA FA-IN A’ZAABAN TAYNA MINKUNNA FA A’LAYHINNA NESFU MAA A’LAL AL-MUHSANAATE MENAL A’ZAABE ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y KHASHEAAA AL-A’ANATA MINKUM WA TASBEROOA KHAYRUL LAKUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nIf any of you have not the means wherewith to wed free believing women, they may wed believing girls from among those whom your right hands possess: And Allah hath full knowledge about your faith. Ye are one from another: Wed them with the leave of their owners, and give them their dowers, according to what is reasonable: They should be chaste, not lustful, nor taking paramours: when they are taken in wedlock, if they fall into shame, their punishment is half that for free women. This (permission) is for those among you who fear sin; but it is better for you that ye practise self-restraint. And Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ سُنَنَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَيَتُوْبَ عَلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(26)\nYOREEDO LAAHO LEEBAYNA LAKUM WA YAHDEYAKUM SUNANA LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM WA YATOOBAL A’LAYKUM WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAllah doth wish to make clear to you and to show you the ordinances of those before you; and (He doth wish to) turn to you (In Mercy): And Allah is All-knowing, All-wise. \nوَاللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّتُوْبَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَيُرِيْدُ الَّذِيْنَ يَتَّبِعُوْنَ الشَّهَوٰتِ اَنْ تَمِيْلُوْا مَيْلًا عَظِيْمًا‏(27)\nWAL LAAHO YOREEDO AN YYATOOBA A’LAYKUM WA YOREEDO LAZEENA YATTABEU’OONA ASH-SHAHAWTE AN TAMEELOOA MAYLAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAllah doth wish to Turn to you, but the wish of those who follow their lusts is that ye should turn away (from Him), far, far away. \nيُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يُّخَفِّفَ عَنْكُمْۚ وَخُلِقَ الْاِنْسَانُ ضَعِيْفًا‏(28)\nYOREEDO LAAHO AN YYUKHAFFEFA A’NKUM WA KHOLEQA INSAANO HAQQO.\nAllah doth wish to lighten your (difficulties): For man was created Weak (in flesh). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَاْكُلُوْۤا اَمْوَالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْبَاطِلِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ تِجَارَةً عَنْ تَرَاضٍ مِّنْكُمْ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيْمًا‏(29)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAAKULOOA AMWAALAKUM BAYNAKUM BIL-BAATELE ILLAA AN TAKOONA TEJAARATAN A’N TARAAZIM MINKUM WA LAA TAQTULOOA FAQTOLOO INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEKUM RAHEEMAA.\nO ye who believe! Eat not up your property among yourselves in vanities: But let there be amongst you Traffic and trade by mutual good-will: Nor kill (or destroy) yourselves: for verily Allah hath been to you Most Merciful! \nوَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ عُدْوَانًا وَّظُلْمًا فَسَوْفَ نُصْلِيْهِ نَارًا ؕ وَكَانَ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرًا‏(30)\nWA MAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA U’UDWAANAN WWAZULMAN FA-SAWFA NUSLEEHE NAARAN KAANAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERAA.\nIf any do that in rancour and injustice, soon shall We cast them into the Fire: And easy it is for Allah. \nاِنْ تَجْتَنِبُوْا كَبٰٓئِرَ مَا تُنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ نُكَفِّرْ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَنُدْخِلْكُمْ مُّدْخَلًا كَرِيْمًا‏(31)\nIN TAJTANEBOOA KABAAAERA MAA TUNHAWNA A’NHO NUKAFFER A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WANUDKHELKUM MMUDKHALAN KAREEMAA.\nIf ye (but) eschew the most heinous of the things which ye are forbidden to do, We shall expel out of you all the evil in you, and admit you to a gate of great honour. \nوَلَا تَتَمَنَّوْا مَا فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ بَعْضَكُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ ؕ لِلرِّجَالِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبُوْا ؕ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا اكْتَسَبْنَ ؕ وَسْئَلُوا اللّٰهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمًا‏(32)\nWA LAA TATAMANNAWA MAA FAZZALA LAAHO BEHI BAA’ZAKUM A’LAA ELAA LELRREJAALE NASEEBUM MIMMAA MAKTASABOO WALELNNESAAE NASEEBUM MIMMAA AKTASABNA WASALOOA LAAHA MIN FAZLEHI INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEMAN.\nAnd in no wise covet those things in which Allah Hath bestowed His gifts More freely on some of you than on others: To men is allotted what they earn, and to women what they earn: But ask Allah of His bounty. For Allah hath full knowledge of all things. \nوَلِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنَا مَوَالِىَ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدٰنِ وَالْاَقْرَبُوْنَ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ عَقَدَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ فَاٰ تُوْهُمْ نَصِيْبَهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدًا ۙ‏(33)\nWA JA-A’LNAA MAWAALEAAA MIMMAA TARAKA AL-WAALEDAANE WAL AAQRABOONA WAL LAZEENA A’AQADAT AYMAANOKUM FA-AATOOHUNNA TOOHUM NASEEBAHUM INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN SHAHEEDAA.\nTo (benefit) every one, We have appointed shares and heirs to property left by parents and relatives. To those, also, to whom your right hand was pledged, give their due portion. For truly Allah is witness to all things. \nاَلرِّجَالُ قَوَّامُوْنَ عَلَى النِّسَآءِ بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّبِمَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا مِنْ اَمْوَالِهِمْ ؕ فَالصّٰلِحٰتُ قٰنِتٰتٌ حٰفِظٰتٌ لِّلْغَيْبِ بِمَا حَفِظَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَالّٰتِىْ تَخَافُوْنَ نُشُوْزَهُنَّ فَعِظُوْهُنَّ وَاهْجُرُوْهُنَّ فِى الْمَضَاجِعِ وَاضْرِبُوْهُنَّ ۚ فَاِنْ اَطَعْنَكُمْ فَلَا تَبْغُوْا عَلَيْهِنَّ سَبِيْلًا ؕاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(34)\nAALRREJAALU QAWAMOONA A’LAL NESAAA-E BEMAA FAZZALA LAAHO BA’ZAHUM A’LAA ELAA WWABEMAA ANFAQOO MIN AAMWAALEHEM FAALSSAALEHAATU QAANETAATUN HAAFEZAATUN LLELGHAYBE BEMAA HAFEZA LAAHO WA KHAALEKA TAKHAAFOONA NUSHOOZAHUNNA FAE’EZOOHUNNA WAAHJUROOHUNNA FIL AL-MAZAAJEE’E WAAZREBOOHUNNA FA-IN AATAA’NAKUM FALAA TABGHOOA A’LAYHINNA SABEELAA AENNA LAAHA KAANA A’ALEEA KABEERAA.\nMen are the protectors and maintainers of women, because Allah has given the one more (strength) than the other, and because they support them from their means. Therefore the righteous women are devoutly obedient, and guard in (the husband's) absence what Allah would have them guard. As to those women on whose part ye fear disloyalty and ill-conduct, admonish them (first), (Next), refuse to share their beds, (And last) beat them (lightly); but if they return to obedience, seek not against them Means (of annoyance): For Allah is Most High, great (above you all). \nوَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ شِقَاقَ بَيْنِهِمَا فَابْعَثُوْا حَكَمًا مِّنْ اَهْلِهٖ وَحَكَمًا مِّنْ اَهْلِهَا ۚ اِنْ يُّرِيْدَاۤ اِصْلَاحًا يُّوَفِّقِ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا خَبِيْرًا‏(35)\nWA KHIFTUM SHEQAAQA BAYNEHEMAA FAABA’ASOOA HAKAMAN MIN AHLEHI WAHAKAMAN MIN AHLEHAA IN YYUREEDAA WA YYOOFFEQE LAAHO BAYNAHOMAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LEEMAN KHABEERAA.\nIf ye fear a breach between them twain, appoint (two) arbiters, one from his family, and the other from hers; if they wish for peace, Allah will cause their reconciliation: For Allah hath full knowledge, and is acquainted with all things. \nوَاعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُشْرِكُوْا بِهٖ شَيْئًا ؕ وَّبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا وَّبِذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَ الْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْجَارِ ذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْجَارِ الْجُنُبِ وَالصَّاحِبِ بِالْجَنْۢبِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۙ وَمَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كَانَ مُخْتَالًا فَخُوْرَا ۙ‏(36)\nWA BODUL LAAHA WA LAA TUSHREKOOA BEHI SHAY-ANW WWABEALWAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW WWABEZEAA QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WA AL-MASAAKEENE WAL JAARE ZIL QURBAA WAL JAARE AL-JUNUBE WAALSSAAHEBE BIL-JANBE WAB SABEELE WA MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MAN KAANA MUKHTAALAN FAKHOORAA.\n Serve Allah, and join not any partners with Him; and do good- to parents, kinsfolk, orphans, those in need, neighbours who are near, neighbours who are strangers, the companion by your side, the wayfarer (ye meet), and what your right hands possess: For Allah loveth not the arrogant, the vainglorious;- \nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يَبْخَلُوْنَ وَيَاْمُرُوْنَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَيَكْتُمُوْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ ؕ وَ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا ۚ‏(37)\nLAZEENA YABKHALOONA WAYAAMUROONA NAASA BIL-BUKHLE WA YAKTOMOONA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WA A-A’TADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\n(Nor) those who are niggardly or enjoin niggardliness on others, or hide the bounties which Allah hath bestowed on them; for We have prepared, for those who resist Faith, a punishment that steeps them in contempt;- \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ رِئَآءَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَلَا بِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ وَمَنْ يَّكُنِ الشَّيْطٰنُ لَهٗ قَرِيْنًا فَسَآءَ قَرِيْنًا‏(38)\nWAL LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM LAHU NAASE WA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA LAA BE-YAWME AAKHER WA MAN YYAKUNE SHAYTAANO LAHU QAREENAN FA-SAAA-A QAREENAN.\nNot those who spend of their substance, to be seen of men, but have no faith in Allah and the Last Day: If any take the Evil One for their intimate, what a dreadful intimate he is! \nوَمَاذَا عَلَيْهِمْ لَوْ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَاَنْفَقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِهِمْ عَلِيْمًا‏(39)\nWA MAA A’LAYHIM LAW AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA ANFAQOO MIMMAA RAZAQAHUMU LAAHO KAANAL LAAHO BEHIM A’LEEMAN.\nAnd what burden Were it on them if they had faith in Allah and in the Last Day, and they spent out of what Allah hath given them for sustenance? For Allah hath full knowledge of them. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ ۚ وَاِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً يُّضٰعِفْهَا وَيُؤْتِ مِنْ لَّدُنْهُ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًاؔ‏(40)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAZLEMU MISQAALA ZARRATIN WA TAKU HASANATANW YYUZAAE’EFHAA WAYUTE MIN LLADUNHU AJRAN A’AZEEMAN.\nAllah is never unjust in the least degree: If there is any good (done), He doubleth it, and giveth from His own presence a great reward. \nفَكَيْفَ اِذَا جِئْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ اُمَّةٍ ۭ بِشَهِيْدٍ وَّجِئْنَا بِكَ عَلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شَهِيْدًا ؕ‏(41)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA JENAA MIN KULLE UMMATIN BE-SHAHEED WWAJENAA BEKA A’LAA HAAOOLAAA-E SHAHEEDAA.\nHow then if We brought from each people a witness, and We brought thee as a witness against these people! \nيَوْمَئِذٍ يَّوَدُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَعَصَوُا الرَّسُوْلَ لَوْ تُسَوّٰى بِهِمُ الْاَرْضُ ؕ وَلَا يَكْتُمُوْنَ اللّٰهَ حَدِيْثًا‏(42)\nYAWMA-EZIN YYAWADDU LAZEENA KAFAROO WAA’ASAWUA YATTABE-U’R LAW TUSAWAA BEHEMUL ARZO WA LAA YAKTOMOONA LAAHA HADEESAN.\nOn that day those who reject Faith and disobey the messenger will wish that the earth Were made one with them: But never will they hide a single fact from Allah! \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَنْتُمْ سُكَارٰى حَتّٰى تَعْلَمُوْا مَا تَقُوْلُوْنَ وَلَا جُنُبًا اِلَّا عَابِرِىْ سَبِيْلٍ حَتّٰى تَغْتَسِلُوْا ؕ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضٰۤى اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ اَوْ جَآءَ اَحَدٌ مِّنْكُمْ مِّنَ الْغَآئِطِ اَوْ لٰمَسْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوْا مَآءً فَتَيَمَّمُوْا صَعِيْدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوْا بِوُجُوْهِكُمْ وَاَيْدِيْكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا غَفُوْرًا‏(43)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAQRABOOA SALAATA WA ANTUM SUKAARAA HATTAA TA’LAMOO MAA TAQOOLOONA WA LAA JUNUBAN ILLAA A’AABEREAA SABEELIN HATTAA TAGHTASELOOA WA KUNTUM MARZAA AW A’LAA SAFARIN AW JAAA-A AHAD MINKUM MENAL AL-GHAAETE AW LAAMASTUMU NESAAA-A FALAM WA LAM MAAA-AN FATAYAMMAMOOA SAE’EEDAN TAYYEBAA FAAMSAHOOA BEWUJOOHEKUM WA AYDEEKUM INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’AFOOA GHAFOORAR.\nO ye who believe! Approach not prayers with a mind befogged, until ye can understand all that ye say, nor in a state of ceremonial impurity (Except when travelling on the road), until after washing your whole body. If ye are ill, or on a journey, or one of you cometh from offices of nature, or ye have been in contact with women, and ye find no water, then take for yourselves clean sand or earth, and rub therewith your faces and hands. For Allah doth blot out sins and forgive again and again. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ يَشْتَرُوْنَ الضَّلٰلَةَ وَيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَضِلُّوا السَّبِيْلَ ؕ‏(44)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA OOTOO NASEEBAN MENAL KETAABE YASHTAROONA ZALAALATA WA YOREEDOONA AN TAZELLOOA SABEELA.\nHast thou not turned Thy vision to those who were given a portion of the Book? they traffic in error, and wish that ye should lose the right path. \nوَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِاَعْدَآئِكُمْؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ نَصِيْرًا‏(45)\nWAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEAAA’DAAEKUM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WALIYYANW WWAKAFAA BIL-LAAHE NASEERAA.\nBut Allah hath full knowledge of your enemies: Allah is enough for a protector, and Allah is enough for a Helper. \nمِنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا يُحَرِّفُوْنَ الْكَلِمَ عَنْ مَّوَاضِعِهٖ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا وَاسْمَعْ غَيْرَ مُسْمَعٍ وَّرَاعِنَا لَيًّۢا بِاَ لْسِنَتِهِمْ وَطَعْنًا فِىْ الدِّيْنِ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا وَاسْمَعْ وَانْظُرْنَا لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ وَاَقْوَمَ ۙ وَ لٰكِنْ لَّعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(46)\nMENAL LAZEENA HAADOO YUHARREFOONA AL-KALEMA A’N MMAWAAZEE’EH WA YAQOOLOONA SAMEA’NAA WA WAASMAA’ GHAYRA MUSMAA’IN WWARAAE’ENAA LAYA BE-AFWAAHEKUM LSENATEHEM WATAA’NAN FEE DEENE WA LAW ANNAHUM QAALOO SAMEA’NAA WA ATA’NAA WAASMAA’ WA ZURNAA LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM WAAQWAMA WA LAAKEN LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO BEKUFREHIM FALAA YOAMENOONA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nOf the Jews there are those who displace words from their (right) places, and say: “We hear and we disobey”; and “Hear what is not Heard”; and “Ra'ina”; with a twist of their tongues and a slander to Faith. If only they had said: “What hear and we obey”; and “Do hear”; and “Do look at us”; it would have been better for them, and more proper; but Allah hath cursed them for their Unbelief; and but few of them will believe. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ اٰمِنُوْا بِمَا نَزَّلْنَا مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ نَّطْمِسَ وُجُوْهًا فَنَرُدَّهَا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهَاۤ اَوْ نَلْعَنَهُمْ كَمَا لَعَنَّاۤ اَصْحٰبَ السَّبْتِؕ وَكَانَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ مَفْعُوْلًا‏(47)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA AAMENOO BEMAA NAZZALNAA MOSADDEQAL LEMAA MA-A’KUM MIN QABLE AN NNATMESA WUJOOHAN FANARUDDAHAA A’LAA AADBAAREHAA AW NALA’ANAHUM KAMAA LAA’ANNAA MASALAN AS-SABTE KAANAL AMRUL LAAHE MAF-O’OLAA.\nO ye People of the Book! believe in what We have (now) revealed, confirming what was (already) with you, before We change the face and fame of some (of you) beyond all recognition, and turn them hindwards, or curse them as We cursed the Sabbath-breakers, for the decision of Allah Must be carried out. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ اَنْ يُّشْرَكَ بِهٖ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرٰۤى اِثْمًا عَظِيْمًا‏(48)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAGHFERO AN YYUSHRAKA BEHI WA YAGHFERO MAA DOONA ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAQADEH TARAA ISMAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAllah forgiveth not that partners should be set up with Him; but He forgiveth anything else, to whom He pleaseth; to set up partners with Allah is to devise a sin Most heinous indeed. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُزَكُّوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ؕ بَلِ اللّٰهُ يُزَكِّىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(49)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YUZAKKOONA ANFOSAHUM BALIL LAAHO YUZAKKEAA MAN YASHAAA-O WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nHast thou not turned Thy vision to those who claim sanctity for themselves? Nay-but Allah Doth sanctify whom He pleaseth. But never will they fail to receive justice in the least little thing. \nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَؕ وَكَفٰى بِهٖۤ اِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(50)\nAUNZUR KAYFA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA KAFAA BEHI ISMAN MOBEENAA.\nBehold! how they invent a lie against Allah! but that by itself is a manifest sin! \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْجِبْتِ وَالطَّاغُوْتِ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ اَهْدٰى مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا سَبِيْلًا‏(51)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA OOTOO NASEEBAN MENAL KETAABE YOAMENOONA BIL-JEBTE WAALTTAAGHOOTE WA YAQOOLOONA LILLAZEENA KAFAROO HAAOOLAAA-E AHDAA MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SABEELAA.\nHast thou not turned Thy vision to those who were given a portion of the Book? they believe in sorcery and Evil, and say to the Unbelievers that they are better guided in the (right) way Than the believers! \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّلْعَنِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ نَصِيْرًا ؕ‏(52)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO WA MAN YYALA’ANE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU NASEERAA.\nThey are (men) whom Allah hath cursed: And those whom Allah Hath cursed, thou wilt find, have no one to help. \nاَمْ لَهُمْ نَصِيْبٌ مِّنَ الْمُلْكِ فَاِذًا لَّا يُؤْتُوْنَ النَّاسَ نَقِيْرًا ۙ‏(53)\nAM LAHUM NASEEBUM MENAL AL-MULKE FA EZAL LAA YOATOONAZ NAASA NAQEERAN.\nHave they a share in dominion or power? Behold, they give not a farthing to their fellow-men? \nاَمْ يَحْسُدُوْنَ النَّاسَ عَلٰى مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖۚ فَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَاۤ اٰلَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مُّلْكًا عَظِيْمًا‏(54)\nAM YAHSUDOONA NAASA A’LAA MAA AAATAAHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI FAQAD AATAYNAA AALA IBRAAHEEMA KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA AATAYNAAHUM MMULKAN A’ZEEMAA.\nOr do they envy mankind for what Allah hath given them of his bounty? but We had already given the people of Abraham the Book and Wisdom, and conferred upon them a great kingdom. \nفَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اٰمَنَ بِهٖ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ صَدَّ عَنْهُ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِجَهَنَّمَ سَعِيْرًا‏(55)\nFA-MINHUM MAN AAMANA BEHI WA MINHUM MAN SADDA A’NHO KAFAA YAWMAEZIM SA-E’ERAA.\nSome of them believed, and some of them averted their faces from him: And enough is Hell for a burning fire. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا سَوْفَ نُصْلِيْهِمْ نَارًا ؕ كُلَّمَا نَضِجَتْ جُلُوْدُهُمْ بَدَّلْنٰهُمْ جُلُوْدًا غَيْرَهَا لِيَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(56)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENAA SAWFA NUSLEEHEM NAARAN KULLAMAA NAZEJAT JULOODUHUM BADDALNAAHUM JULOODAN GHAYRAHAA LEEZOOQOOA A’ZAABA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\nThose who reject our Signs, We shall soon cast into the Fire: as often as their skins are roasted through, We shall change them for fresh skins, that they may taste the penalty: for Allah is Exalted in Power, Wise. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ لَهُمْ فِيْهَاۤ اَزْوَاجٌ مُّطَهَّرَةٌ  وَّنُدْخِلُهُمْ ظِلًّا ظَلِيْلًا‏(57)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SANUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM LAHUM FEEHAA AZWAAJUM MOTAHHARATUNW WWANUDKHELUHUM ZELLAN ZALEELAN.\nBut those who believe and do deeds of righteousness, We shall soon admit to Gardens, with rivers flowing beneath, their eternal home: Therein shall they have companions pure and holy: We shall admit them to shades, cool and ever deepening. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْمُرُكُمْ اَنْ تُؤَدُّوا الْاَمٰنٰتِ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهَا ۙ وَاِذَا حَكَمْتُمْ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ اَنْ تَحْكُمُوْا بِالْعَدْلِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ نِعِمَّا يَعِظُكُمْ بِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ سَمِيْعًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(58)\nINNAL LAAHA YAAMOROKUM AN TUADDOOA AL-AAMAANAATE ELAA AHLEHAA WA EZAA HAKAMTUM BAYNA NAASE AN TAHKUMOOA BIL-A’DL INNAL LAAHA NEE’EMMAA YA-E’ZOKUM BEHI INNAL LAAHA KAANA SAMEE-A’M BASEERAA.\n Allah doth command you to render back your Trusts to those to whom they are due; And when ye judge between man and man, that ye judge with justice: Verily how excellent is the teaching which He giveth you! For Allah is He Who heareth and seeth all things. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَاُولِى الْاَمْرِ مِنْكُمْۚ فَاِنْ تَنَازَعْتُمْ فِىْ شَىْءٍ فَرُدُّوْهُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَالرَّسُوْلِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَحْسَنُ تَاْوِيْلًا‏(59)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R WA ULIL AL-AAMRE MINKUM FA-IN TANAAZAA’TUM FEE SHAY-IN FARUDDOOHU ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLE IN KUNTUM TUMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL WWAAHSANU TAAWEELAN.\nO ye who believe! Obey Allah, and obey the Messenger, and those charged with authority among you. If ye differ in anything among yourselves, refer it to Allah and His Messenger, if ye do believe in Allah and the Last Day: That is best, and most suitable for final determination. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَزْعُمُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ اٰمَنُوْا بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَحَاكَمُوْۤا اِلَى الطَّاغُوْتِ وَقَدْ اُمِرُوْۤا اَنْ يَّكْفُرُوْا بِهٖ ؕ وَيُرِيْدُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَنْ يُّضِلَّهُمْ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(60)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YAZU’UMOONA ANNAHUM AAMANOO BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLEKA YOREEDOONA AN YYATAHAAKAMOOA ELAL AT-TAAGHOOTE WA QAD MAAA OMEROO AN YYAKFUROOA BEHI WA YOREEDO SHAYTAANO AN YYUZELLAHUM ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nHast thou not turned Thy vision to those who declare that they believe in the revelations that have come to thee and to those before thee? Their (real) wish is to resort together for judgment (in their disputes) to the Evil One, though they were ordered to reject him. But Satan's wish is to lead them astray far away (from the right). \nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ وَاِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ رَاَيْتَ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْكَ صُدُوْدًا ۚ‏(61)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM TA-A’ALAW ELAA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO WA ELAL RASOOLE RA-AYTA MONAAFEQEENA YASUDDOONA A’NKAL SUDOODAN.\nWhen it is said to them: “Come to what Allah hath revealed, and to the Messenger”: Thou seest the Hypocrites avert their faces from thee in disgust. \nفَكَيْفَ اِذَاۤ اَصَابَتْهُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ ۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ ثُمَّ جَآءُوْكَ يَحْلِفُوْنَۖ بِاللّٰهِ اِنْ اَرَدْنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِحْسَانًا وَّتَوْفِيْقًا‏(62)\nFA-KAYFA EZAA ASAABATHUM MOSEEBATUN BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM SUMMA JAAOOKA YAHLEFOONA BIL-LAAHE IN AARADNAA ILLAA EHSAANANW WWATAWFEEQAN.\nHow then, when they are seized by misfortune, because of the deeds which they hands have sent forth? Then their come to thee, swearing by Allah: “We meant no more than good-will and conciliation!” \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْلَمُ اللّٰهُ مَا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَعِظْهُمْ وَقُلْ لَّهُمْ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ قَوْلًاۢ بَلِيْغًا‏(63)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA YA’LAMO LAAHO MAA FEE QOLOOBEHIM FAAA’REZ A’NHUM WAE’EZHUM WA QUL LAHUM FEE ANFOSEHIM QAWLAM BALEEGHAN.\nThose men, Allah knows what is in their hearts; so keep clear of them, but admonish them, and speak to them a word to reach their very souls. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا لِيُطَاعَ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اِذْ ظَّلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ جَآءُوْكَ فَاسْتَغْفَرُوا اللّٰهَ وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ الرَّسُوْلُ لَوَجَدُوا اللّٰهَ تَوَّابًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(64)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN RASOOLIN ILLAA LEETAAA’A BE-IZNIL LAAHE WA LAW ANNAHUM IZ ZZALAMOOA ANFOSAHUM JAAOOKA FAASTAGHFAROOA LAAHA WAASTAGHFARA LAHOMUL RASOOLO LAWAJADOOA LAAHA TAWWAABAA RAHEEMAA.\nWe sent not a messenger, but to be obeyed, in accordance with the will of Allah. If they had only, when they were unjust to themselves, come unto thee and asked Allah's forgiveness, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah indeed Oft-returning, Most Merciful. \nفَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ حَتّٰى يُحَكِّمُوْكَ فِيْمَا شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَجِدُوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجًا مِّمَّا قَضَيْتَ وَيُسَلِّمُوْا تَسْلِيْمًا‏(65)\nFALAA WA RABBEKA LAA YOAMENOONA HATTAA YUHAKKEMOOKA FEEMAA SHAJARA BAYNAHUM SUMMA LAA YAJEDOOA FEE ANFOSEHIM HARAJAN MIMMAA QAZAYTA WAYUSALLEMOOA TASLEEMAA.\nBut no, by the Lord, they can have no (real) Faith, until they make thee judge in all disputes between them, and find in their souls no resistance against Thy decisions, but accept them with the fullest conviction. \nوَلَوْ اَنَّا كَتَبْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَنِ اقْتُلُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ اَوِ اخْرُجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِكُمْ مَّا فَعَلُوْهُ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ مِّنْهُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ فَعَلُوْا مَا يُوْعَظُوْنَ بِهٖ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَّهُمْ وَاَشَدَّ تَثْبِيْتًا ۙ‏(66)\nWA LAW ANNAA KATABNAA A’LAYHIM SAALEHAN AQTULOOA ANFOSAKUM AWE’ AKHRUJOOA MIN DEYAAREKUM MAA FAA’ALOOHU ILLAA QALEELUN MINHUM WA LAW ANNAHUM FAA’ALOOA MAA YOOA’AZOONA BEHI LAKAANA KHAYRAN LAHUM WA ASHADDA TASBEETAM.\nIf We had ordered them to sacrifice their lives or to leave their homes, very few of them would have done it: But if they had done what they were (actually) told, it would have been best for them, and would have gone farthest to strengthen their (faith); \nوَّاِذًا لَّاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ لَّدُنَّاۤ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(67)\nWWAAZAN LLAATAYNAAHUM MIN WA AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nAnd We should then have given them from our presence a great reward; \nوَّلَهَدَيْنٰهُمْ صِرَاطًا مُّسْتَقِيْمًا‏(68)\nWWALAHADAYNAAHUM SERAATAM MUSTAQEEMAA.\nAnd We should have shown them the Straight Way. \nوَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ وَالصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ وَالشُّهَدَآءِ وَالصّٰلِحِيْنَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ رَفِيْقًا ؕ‏(69)\nWA MAN YOTE-I’L LAAHA WA YATTABE-U’R FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAAHA LAZEENA AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYHIM MENAL NABIYYEENA WAALSSEDDEEQEENA WA AN WA SAALEHEEN WAHASUNA OOLAAA-EKA RAFEEQAN.\nAll who obey Allah and the messenger are in the company of those on whom is the Grace of Allah, of the prophets (who teach), the sincere (lovers of Truth), the witnesses (who testify), and the Righteous (who do good): Ah! what a beautiful fellowship! \nذٰ لِكَ الْفَضْلُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ عَلِيْمًا‏(70)\nZAA LEKA FAZLUL MENAL LAAHE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE A’LEEMAN.\nSuch is the bounty from Allah: And sufficient is it that Allah knoweth all. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا خُذُوْا حِذْرَكُمْ فَانْفِرُوْا ثُبَاتٍ اَوِ انْفِرُوْا جَمِيْعًا‏(71)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KHOZOO HEZRAKUM FAANFEROOA SUBAATIN AWE’ ANFEROOA JAMEE-A’A.\nO ye who believe! Take your precautions, and either go forth in parties or go forth all together. \nوَاِنَّ مِنْكُمْ لَمَنْ لَّيُبَطِّئَنَّۚ فَاِنْ اَصَابَتْكُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ قَالَ قَدْ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَىَّ اِذْ لَمْ اَكُنْ مَّعَهُمْ شَهِيْدًا‏(72)\nWA INNA MINKUM LAMAN LLAYUBATTEANNA FA-IN AASAABATKUM MOSEEBATUN QAALA QAD AN-A’MAL LAAHO A’LAYYA IZ LAM AAKUN MMAA’AHUM SHAHEEDAA.\nThere are certainly among you men who would tarry behind: If a misfortune befalls you, they say: “Allah did favour us in that we were not present among them.” \nوَلَئِنْ اَصَابَكُمْ فَضْلٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ كَاَنْ لَّمْ تَكُنْۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهٗ مَوَدَّةٌ يّٰلَيْتَنِىْ كُنْتُ مَعَهُمْ فَاَ فُوْزَ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا‏(73)\nWA LAIN AASAABAKUM FAZLUN MENAL LAAHE LAYAQOOLANNA KA-AN LAM TAKUN BAYNAKUM BAYNAHU MAWADDATUN YYAALAYTANEAA KUNTO MA-A’HUM FA-ALQEEHE FOOZA FAWZAN A’ZEEMAA.\nBut if good fortune comes to you from Allah, they would be sure to say - as if there had never been Ties of affection between you and them - “Oh! I wish I had been with them; a fine thing should I then have made of it!” \nفَلْيُقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْنَ يَشْرُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا بِالْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَيُقْتَلْ اَوْ يَغْلِبْ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيْهِ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(74)\nFALYUQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAZEENA YASHROONA HAYAATAD DUNYAA BIL AAKHERATE WA MAN YYUQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FAYUQTAL AW YAGHLEB FA-SAWFA NUTEEHE AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\n Let those fight in the cause of Allah Who sell the life of this world for the hereafter. To him who fighteth in the cause of Allah, whether he is slain or gets victory - Soon shall We give him a reward of great (value). \nوَمَا لَكُمْ لَا تُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَآءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ الَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا مِنْ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ الظَّالِمِ اَهْلُهَا ۚ وَاجْعَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا ۙۚ وَّاجْعَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ نَصِيْرًا ؕ‏(75)\nWA MAA LAKUM LAA TUQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AR-REJAALE WA NESAAA-E WAL WELDAANE LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAKHREJNAA MIN HAAZEHE QARYAH AZ-ZAALEME AAHLUHAA WA A’L LANAA MIN LLADUNKA WALIYYANW WWAAJA’AL LANAA MIN LLADUNKA NASEERAA.\nAnd why should ye not fight in the cause of Allah and of those who, being weak, are ill-treated (and oppressed)? Men, women, and children, whose cry is: “Our Lord! Rescue us from this town, whose people are oppressors; and raise for us from thee one who will protect; and raise for us from thee one who will help!” \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ الطَّاغُوْتِ فَقَاتِلُوْۤا اَوْلِيَآءَ الشَّيْطٰنِۚ اِنَّ كَيْدَ الشَّيْطٰنِ كَانَ ضَعِيْفًا‏(76)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL AT-TAAGHOOTE FAQAATELOOA AAWLEEAAAA SHAYTAANE INNAL KAYDA SHAYTAANE KAANA HAQQO.\nThose who believe fight in the cause of Allah, and those who reject Faith Fight in the cause of Evil: So fight ye against the friends of Satan: feeble indeed is the cunning of Satan. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ كُفُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰ تُوا الزَّكٰوةَ ۚ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتَالُ اِذَا فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ يَخْشَوْنَ النَّاسَ كَخَشْيَةِ اللّٰهِ اَوْ اَشَدَّ خَشْيَةً ۚ وَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لِمَ كَتَبْتَ عَلَيْنَا الْقِتَالَ ۚ لَوْلَاۤ اَخَّرْتَنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ قَرِيْبٍ ؕ قُلْ مَتَاعُ الدُّنْيَا قَلِيْلٌ ۚ وَالْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنِ اتَّقٰى وَلَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(77)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA QEELA LAHUM KUFFOOA AAYDEEKUM WA AQEEMUS SALAATA WAA TOOA ZAKAATA FALAMMAA KOTEBA A’LAYHEMUL QETAALO EZAA FAREEQUM MINHUM YAKHSHAWNA NAASA KA-KHASYATIL LAAHE AW ASHADDA KHASHYATAN WA QAALOO RABBANAA LEMA KATABTA A’LAYNAA QETAAL LAWLAA AAKKHARTANAA ELAA ELAA QAREEBIN QUL MATAAU’U DUNYAA QALEELUN WAL AAKHERATO KHAYRUL LLEMANE WAA WA LAA TUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nHast thou not turned Thy vision to those who were told to hold back their hands (from fight) but establish regular prayers and spend in regular charity? When (at length) the order for fighting was issued to them, behold! a section of them feared men as - or even more than - they should have feared Allah: They said: “Our Lord! Why hast Thou ordered us to fight? Wouldst Thou not Grant us respite to our (natural) term, near (enough)?” Say: “Short is the enjoyment of this world: the Hereafter is the best for those who do right: Never will ye be dealt with unjustly in the very least! \nاَيْنَ مَا تَكُوْنُوْا يُدْرِكْكُّمُ الْمَوْتُ وَلَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ بُرُوْجٍ مُّشَيَّدَةٍ ؕ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ حَسَنَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا هٰذِهٖ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَّقُوْلُوْا هٰذِهٖ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ ؕ قُلْ كُلٌّ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَمَالِ ھٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ الْقَوْمِ لَا يَكَادُوْنَ يَفْقَهُوْنَ حَدِيْثًا‏(78)\nAYNA MAA TAKOONOO YUDREKKKUMU MAWTO WA LAW KUNTUM FEE BUROOJIN MMUSHAYDATIN WA IN TOSIBHUM HASANATUL YAQOOLOO HAAZEHI MIN I’NDIL LAAHE WA IN TOSIBHUM SAYYE-ATUM YAQOOLOO HAAZEHI MIN I’NDEK QUL KULLUL MIN I’NDIL LAAHE FAMAALE ULAAE QAWMIL LAA YAKAADOONA YAFQAHOON HADEESAN.\n“Wherever ye are, death will find you out, even if ye are in towers built up strong and high!” If some good befalls them, they say, “This is from Allah”; but if evil, they say, “This is from thee” (O Prophet). Say: “All things are from Allah.” But what hath come to these people, that they fail to understand a single fact? \nمَاۤ اَصَابَكَ مِنْ حَسَنَةٍ فَمِنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَصَابَكَ مِنْ سَيِّئَةٍ فَمِنْ نَّفْسِكَ ؕ وَاَرْسَلْنٰكَ لِلنَّاسِ رَسُوْلًا ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًا‏(79)\nMAA AASAABAKA MIN HASANATIN NAASE LAAHE WA MAA AASAABAKA MIN SAYATIN FAMIN NNAFSEKA WA ARSALNAAKA LIN-NAASE RASOOLAM KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA.\nWhatever good, (O man!) happens to thee, is from Allah; but whatever evil happens to thee, is from thy (own) soul. and We have sent thee as a messenger to (instruct) mankind. And enough is Allah for a witness. \nمَنْ يُّطِعِ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدْ اَطَاعَ اللّٰهَ ۚ وَمَنْ تَوَلّٰى فَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا ؕ‏(80)\nMAN YOTE-I’L YATTABE-U’R FAQAD AATAAA’A LAAHA WA MAN TAWALLAA FAMAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN.\nHe who obeys the Messenger, obeys Allah: But if any turn away, We have not sent thee to watch over their (evil deeds). \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ طَاعَةٌ فَاِذَا بَرَزُوْا مِنْ عِنْدِكَ بَيَّتَ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ تَقُوْلُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَكْتُبُ مَا يُبَيِّتُوْنَ ۚ فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(81)\nWA YAQOOLOONA TAAA’ATUN FA-EZAA BARAZOO MIN I’NDEK BAYTA TAAEFATUN MINHUM GHAYRA LAZEE TAQOOLO WAL LAAHO YAKTUBU MAA YUBAYTOONA FAAA’REZ A’NHUM WA TAWAKKAL A’LAL LAAHE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nThey have “Obedience” on their lips; but when they leave thee, a section of them Meditate all night on things very different from what thou tellest them. But Allah records their nightly (plots): So keep clear of them, and put thy trust in Allah, and enough is Allah as a disposer of affairs. \nاَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُوْنَ الْقُرْاٰنَؕ وَلَوْ كَانَ مِنْ عِنْدِ غَيْرِ اللّٰهِ لَوَجَدُوْا فِيْهِ اخْتِلَافًا كَثِيْرًا‏(82)\nAFALAA YATADABBAROONA QURAAN WA LAW KAANA MIN I’NDIL GHAIRE LAAHE LAWAJADOOA FEEHE AKHTELAAFAN KASEERAA.\nDo they not consider the Qur'an (with care)? Had it been from other Than Allah, they would surely have found therein Much discrepancy. \nوَاِذَا جَآءَهُمْ اَمْرٌ مِّنَ الْاَمْنِ اَوِ الْخَوْفِ اَذَاعُوْا بِهٖ ۚ وَلَوْ رَدُّوْهُ اِلَى الرَّسُوْلِ وَاِلٰٓى اُولِى الْاَمْرِ مِنْهُمْ لَعَلِمَهُ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَنْۢبِطُوْنَهٗ مِنْهُمْؕ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ لَاتَّبَعْتُمُ الشَّيْطٰنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(83)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AHUM AAMRUN MENAL AL-AAMNE AWE’ KHAWFE AAZAAU’OOA BEHI WA LAW RADDOOHU ELAL RASOOLE WA ELAA ULIL AL-AAMRE MINHUM LAA’ALEMAHU LAZEENA YASTANBETOONAH MENHUM WA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU LAATTABAA’TUMU ASH-SHAYTAANA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nWhen there comes to them some matter touching (Public) safety or fear, they divulge it. If they had only referred it to the Messenger, or to those charged with authority among them, the proper investigators would have Tested it from them (direct). Were it not for the Grace and Mercy of Allah unto you, all but a few of you would have fallen into the clutches of Satan. \nفَقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ۚ لَا تُكَلَّفُ اِلَّا نَفْسَكَ وَحَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ۚ عَسَے اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّكُفَّ بَاْسَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَشَدُّ بَاْسًا وَّاَشَدُّ تَنْكِيْلًا‏(84)\nFAQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAA TOKALLAFO ILLAA NAFSAKA WAHARREZE MOAMENEEN A’ASA LAAHO AN YYAKUFFA BAASA LAZEENA KAFAROO WAL LAAHO ASHADDO BAASAN WWAASHADDU TANKEELAN.\nThen fight in Allah's cause - Thou art held responsible only for thyself - and rouse the believers. It may be that Allah will restrain the fury of the Unbelievers; for Allah is the strongest in might and in punishment. \nمَنْ يَّشْفَعْ شَفَاعَةً حَسَنَةً يَّكُنْ لَّهٗ نَصِيْبٌ مِّنْهَا ۚ وَمَنْ يَّشْفَعْ شَفَاعَةً سَيِّئَةً يَّكُنْ لَّهٗ كِفْلٌ مِّنْهَا ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّقِيْتًا‏(85)\nMAN YYASHFAA’ SHAFAAA’ATAN HASANATANW YYAKUN LAHU NASEEBUM MINHAA WA MAN YYASHFAA’ SHAFAAA’ATAN SAYYE-ATANW YYAKUN LAHU KEFLUN MINHAA KAANAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN MMUQEETAN.\nWhoever recommends and helps a good cause becomes a partner therein: And whoever recommends and helps an evil cause, shares in its burden: And Allah hath power over all things. \nوَاِذَا حُيِّيْتُمْ بِتَحِيَّةٍ فَحَيُّوْا بِاَحْسَنَ مِنْهَاۤ اَوْ رُدُّوْهَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَسِيْبًا‏(86)\nWA EZAA HUYYEETUM BETAHEETIN FAHAYWA BE-AHSANAL MINHAA AW RUDDOOHAA INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HASEEBAA.\nWhen a (courteous) greeting is offered you, meet it with a greeting still more courteous, or (at least) of equal courtesy. Allah takes careful account of all things. \nاللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِؕ وَمَنْ اَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ حَدِيْثًا‏(87)\nLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO LAYAJMAA’ANNAKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEH WA MAN AASDAQU MENAL LAAHE HADEESAN.\nAllah! There is no god but He: of a surety He will gather you together against the Day of Judgment, about which there is no doubt. And whose word can be truer than Allah's? \nفَمَا لَكُمْ فِىْ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ فِئَتَيْنِ وَاللّٰهُ اَرْكَسَهُمْ بِمَا كَسَبُوْاؕ اَ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَهْدُوْا مَنْ اَضَلَّ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ سَبِيْلًا‏(88)\nFAMAA LAKUM FEE MONAAFEQEENA FEATAYNE WAL LAAHO AARKASAHUM BEMAA KASABOOA A’ZAABAN TOREEDOONA AN TAHDOOA MAN AZALLAL LAAHO WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU SABEELAA.\n Why should ye be divided into two parties about the Hypocrites? Allah hath upset them for their (evil) deeds. Would ye guide those whom Allah hath thrown out of the Way? For those whom Allah hath thrown out of the Way, never shalt thou find the Way. \nوَدُّوْا لَوْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ كَمَا كَفَرُوْا فَتَكُوْنُوْنَ سَوَآءً فَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ حَتّٰى يُهَاجِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ؕ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوْهُمْ حَيْثُ وَجَدتُّمُوْهُمْ وَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْهُمْ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(89)\nWADDOOA LAW TAKFOROONA KAMAA KAFAROO FATAKOONOONA SAWAAAN FALAA TATTAKHEZOOA MINHUM AAWLEEAAAA HATTAA YUHAAJEROOA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FA-IN TAWALLAW FAKHUZOOHUM WAQ TOLOOHUM HAYSO WAJADTTUMOOHUM WA LAA TATTAKHEZOOA MINHUM WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\nThey but wish that ye should reject Faith, as they do, and thus be on the same footing (as they): But take not friends from their ranks until they flee in the way of Allah (From what is forbidden). But if they turn renegades, seize them and slay them wherever ye find them; and (in any case) take no friends or helpers from their ranks;- \nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ يَصِلُوْنَ اِلٰى قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ اَوْ جَآءُوْكُمْ حَصِرَتْ صُدُوْرُهُمْ اَنْ يُّقَاتِلُوْكُمْ اَوْ يُقَاتِلُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَسَلَّطَهُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ فَلَقٰتَلُوْكُمْ ۚ فَاِنِ اعْتَزَلُوْكُمْ فَلَمْ يُقَاتِلُوْكُمْ وَاَلْقَوْا اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ ۙ فَمَا جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سَبِيْلًا‏(90)\nILLAA LAZEENA YASELOONA ELAA QAWMIN BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MMEESAAQUN AW JAAA-OOKUM HASERAT SODOOROHUM AN YYUQAATELOOKUM AW YUQAATELOOA QAWMAHUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LASALLATAHUM A’LAYKUM FALAQAATALOOKUM FA-ENIN AA’TAZALOOKUM FALAM YUQAATELOOKUM WAALQAWA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAMA FAMAA JA-A’LA LAAHO LAKUM A’LAYHIM SABEELAA.\nExcept those who join a group between whom and you there is a treaty (of peace), or those who approach you with hearts restraining them from fighting you as well as fighting their own people. If Allah had pleased, He could have given them power over you, and they would have fought you: Therefore if they withdraw from you but fight you not, and (instead) send you (Guarantees of) peace, then Allah Hath opened no way for you (to war against them). \nسَتَجِدُوْنَ اٰخَرِيْنَ يُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّاْمَنُوْكُمْ وَيَاْمَنُوْا قَوْمَهُمْ ؕ كُلَّمَا رُدُّوْۤا اِلَى الْفِتْنَةِ اُرْكِسُوْا فِيْهَا ۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يَعْتَزِلُوْكُمْ وَيُلْقُوْۤا اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلَمَ وَيَكُفُّوْۤا اَيْدِيَهُمْ فَخُذُوْهُمْ وَاقْتُلُوْهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوْهُمْ ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكُمْ جَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(91)\nSATAJEDOONA AAKHEREEN YOREEDOONA AN YYAAMANOOKUM WAYAAMANOOA QAWMAHUM KULLAMAA RUDDOOA ELAL AL-FETNATE AURKESOOA FEEHAA FA-IN LAM YAA’TAZELOOKUM WAYULQOOA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAMA WAYAKUFFOOA AYDEYAHUM FAKHUZOOHUM WAQ TOLOOHUM HAYSO SAQIFTOMOOHUM WAAWLAAAEKUM JA-A’LNAA LAKUM A’LAYHIM SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nOthers you will find that wish to gain your confidence as well as that of their people: Every time they are sent back to temptation, they succumb thereto: if they withdraw not from you nor give you (guarantees) of peace besides restraining their hands, seize them and slay them wherever ye get them: In their case We have provided you with a clear argument against them. \nوَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ اَنْ يَّقْتُلَ مُؤْمِنًا اِلَّا خَطَئًا ۚ وَمَنْ قَتَلَ مُؤْمِنًا خَطَئًا فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ وَّدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّصَّدَّقُوْا ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَدُوٍّ لَّكُمْ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَ مِنْ قَوْمٍۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ مِّيْثَاقٌ فَدِيَةٌ مُّسَلَّمَةٌ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ وَ تَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مُّؤْمِنَةٍ ۚ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ تَوْبَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(92)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-MOAMENINW AN YYAQTULA MUMENAN ILLAA KHATAAN WA MAN QATALA MUMENAN KHATAAN FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN WWADEETUN MMUSALLAMATUN ELAA AHLEHI ILLAA AN YYASSADDAQOOA FA-IN KAANA MIN QAWMIN A’ADOO LAKUM WA HOWA MUMENUN FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN WA KAANA MIN QAWMIN BAYNAKUM WA BAYNAHUM MMEESAAQUN FADEETUN MMUSALLAMATUN ELAA AHLEHI WA TAHREERU RAQABATIN MMUMENATIN FAMAN LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SHAHRAYNE MUTATAABEA’AYNE TAWBATAN MENAL LAAHE KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nNever should a believer kill a believer; but (If it so happens) by mistake, (Compensation is due): If one (so) kills a believer, it is ordained that he should free a believing slave, and pay compensation to the deceased's family, unless they remit it freely. If the deceased belonged to a people at war with you, and he was a believer, the freeing of a believing slave (Is enough). If he belonged to a people with whom ye have treaty of Mutual alliance, compensation should be paid to his family, and a believing slave be freed. For those who find this beyond their means, (is prescribed) a fast for two months running: by way of repentance to Allah: for Allah hath all knowledge and all wisdom. \nوَمَنْ يَّقْتُلْ مُؤْمِنًا مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَآؤُهٗ جَهَنَّمُ خَالِدًا فِيْهَا وَغَضِبَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهٗ وَاَعَدَّ لَهٗ عَذَابًا عَظِيْمًا‏(93)\nWA MAN YYAQTUL MUMENAN MMUTAA’AMMEDAN FAJAZAAUH JAHANNAMUL KHAALEDAN FEEHAA WA GHAZEBAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WALAA’ANAH WA A-A’DDA LAHU A’ZAABAN A’ZEEMAA.\nIf a man kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, to abide therein (For ever): And the wrath and the curse of Allah are upon him, and a dreadful penalty is prepared for him. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَتَبَيَّنُوْا وَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا لِمَنْ اَ لْقٰٓى اِلَيْكُمُ السَّلٰمَ لَسْتَ مُؤْمِنًا ۚ تَبْتَغُوْنَ عَرَضَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ مَغَانِمُ كَثِيْرَةٌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كُنْتُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ فَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَتَبَيَّنُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(94)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA ZARABTUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE FATABAYNOOA WA LAA TAQOOLOO LEMAN-Y A’ZAABAN LQAAA AELAYKUMU AS-SALAAMA LASTA MUMENAN TABTAGHOONA A’ARAZA HAYAATID DUNYAA FA I’NDAL LAAHE MAGHAANEMU KASEERATUN KAZAALEKA KUNTUM MIN QABLO FAMANNA LAAHO A’LAYKUM FATABAYNOOA INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\nO ye who believe! When ye go abroad in the cause of Allah, investigate carefully, and say not to any one who offers you a salutation: “Thou art none of a believer!” Coveting the perishable goods of this life: with Allah are profits and spoils abundant. Even thus were ye yourselves before, till Allah conferred on you His favours: Therefore carefully investigate. For Allah is well aware of all that ye do. \nلَا يَسْتَوِى الْقَاعِدُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ غَيْرُ اُولِى الضَّرَرِ وَالْمُجَاهِدُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ ؕ فَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ بِاَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاَنْفُسِهِمْ عَلَى الْقٰعِدِيْنَ دَرَجَةً  ؕ وَكُلًّا وَّعَدَ اللّٰهُ الْحُسْنٰىؕ وَفَضَّلَ اللّٰهُ الْمُجٰهِدِيْنَ عَلَى الْقٰعِدِيْنَ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(95)\nLAA YASTAWEAA AL-QAAE’EDOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN GHAYRO ULIL AZ-ZARARE WAL MUJAAHEDOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM FAZZALA LAAHO AL-MUJAAHEDEENA BEAAMWAALEHEM WA ANFOSEHIM A’LAL AL-QAAE’EDEENA DARAJATAN WAKULLAN WWAA’ADA LAAHO HUSNAA WAFAZZALA LAAHO AL-MUJAAHEDEENA A’LAL AL-QAAE’EDEENA AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nNot equal are those believers who sit (at home) and receive no hurt, and those who strive and fight in the cause of Allah with their goods and their persons. Allah hath granted a grade higher to those who strive and fight with their goods and persons than to those who sit (at home). Unto all (in Faith) Hath Allah promised good: But those who strive and fight Hath He distinguished above those who sit (at home) by a special reward, \nدَرَجٰتٍ مِّنْهُ وَمَغْفِرَةً وَّرَحْمَةً ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(96)\nDARAJAATIN MINHO WAMAGHFERATAN WA RAHMATAL KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nRanks specially bestowed by Him, and Forgiveness and Mercy. For Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَوَفّٰٮهُمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ ظَالِمِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ قَالُوْا فِيْمَ كُنْتُمْؕ قَالُوْا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ فِىْ الْاَرْضِؕ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ تَكُنْ اَرْضُ اللّٰهِ وَاسِعَةً فَتُهَاجِرُوْا فِيْهَاؕ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَسَآءَتْ مَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(97)\nINNAL LAZEENA TAWAFFAAHUMU TAHMELOHUL ZAALEMEAA ANFOSEHIM QAALOO FEEMA KUNTUM QAALOO KUNNAA MUSTAZA’AFEENA FEE ARZ QAALOO ALAM TAKUN AARZU LAAHE WAASEA’ATAN FATUHAAJEROOA FEEHAA FA-OOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA SAA-AT MASEERAA.\nWhen angels take the souls of those who die in sin against their souls, they say: “In what (plight) Were ye?” They reply: “Weak and oppressed Were we in the earth.” They say: “Was not the earth of Allah spacious enough for you to move yourselves away (From evil)?” Such men will find their abode in Hell, What an evil refuge! - \nاِلَّا الْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَآءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ حِيْلَةً وَّلَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ سَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(98)\nILLAA AL-MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AR-REJAALE WA NESAAA-E WAL WELDAANE LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA HEELATAN WA LAA YAHTADOON SABEELAA.\nExcept those who are (really) weak and oppressed - men, women, and children - who have no means in their power, nor (a guide-post) to their way. \nفَاُولٰٓئِكَ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَفُوًّا غَفُوْرًا‏(99)\nFA-OOLAAA-EKA A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYAA’FOO A’ANHUM KAANAL LAAHO A’AFOOA GHAFOORAR.\nFor these, there is hope that Allah will forgive: For Allah doth blot out (sins) and forgive again and again. \nوَمَنْ يُّهَاجِرْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ يَجِدْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُرٰغَمًا كَثِيْرًا وَّسَعَةً ؕ وَمَنْ يَّخْرُجْ مِنْۢ بَيْتِهٖ مُهَاجِرًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ ثُمَّ يُدْرِكْهُ الْمَوْتُ فَقَدْ وَقَعَ اَجْرُهٗ عَلَى اللّٰهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(100)\nWA MAN YYUHAAJER FEE SABEELIL LAAHE YAJID FIL ARZE MURAAGHAMAN KASEERAA WWASAA’ATAN WA MAN YYAKHRUJ MIN BAYTEH MUHAAJERAN ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI SUMMA YUDREKHU MAWTO FAQAD WAQA-A’L AJROHU A’LAL LAAHE KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\n He who forsakes his home in the cause of Allah, finds in the earth Many a refuge, wide and spacious: Should he die as a refugee from home for Allah and His Messenger, His reward becomes due and sure with Allah: And Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَاِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ تَقْصُرُوْا مِنَ الصَّلٰوةِ ۖ اِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ اِنَّ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ كَانُوْا لَكُمْ عَدُوًّا مُّبِيْنًا‏(101)\nWA EZAA ZARABTUM FIL ARZE FA-LAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN AN TAQSUROOA MENAL AS-SALAAWTE IN KHIFTUM AN YYAFTENAKUMU LAZEENA KAFAROO INNAL KAAFEREEN KAANOO LAKUM A’DUWWAL MOBEENAA.\nWhen ye travel through the earth, there is no blame on you if ye shorten your prayers, for fear the Unbelievers May attack you: For the Unbelievers are unto you open enemies. \nوَاِذَا كُنْتَ فِيْهِمْ فَاَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ فَلْتَقُمْ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ مَّعَكَ وَلْيَاْخُذُوْۤا اَسْلِحَتَهُمْ فَاِذَا سَجَدُوْا فَلْيَكُوْنُوْا مِنْ وَّرَآئِكُمْ وَلْتَاْتِ طَآئِفَةٌ اُخْرٰى لَمْ يُصَلُّوْا فَلْيُصَلُّوْا مَعَكَ وَلْيَاْخُذُوْا حِذْرَهُمْ وَاَسْلِحَتَهُمْ ۚ وَدَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْ تَغْفُلُوْنَ عَنْ اَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَاَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيْلُوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّيْلَةً وَّاحِدَةً ؕ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِنْ كَانَ بِكُمْ اَ ذًى مِّنْ مَّطَرٍ اَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَّرْضٰۤى اَنْ تَضَعُوْۤا اَسْلِحَتَكُمْ ۚ وَ خُذُوْا حِذْرَكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ اَعَدَّ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا‏(102)\nWA EZAA KUNTA FEEHIM FAAQAMTA LAHOMUL SALAATA FALTAQUM TAAEFATUN MINHUM BEMAM WALYAAKHUZOOA AASLEHATAHUM FA-EZAA SAJADOOA FALYAKOONOOA MIN WWARAAEKUM WALTAATE TAAEFATUN LAHU LAM YUSALLOOA FALYUSALLOOA MA-A’KA WALYAAKHUZOOA HEZRAHUM WAASLEHATAHUM WADDA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAW TAGHFULOONA A’N AASLEHATEKUM WAAMTEA’ATEKUM FAYAMEELOONA A’LAYKUM MMAYLATAN WAAHEDATAN WA LAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM IN KAANA BEKUM A’ZAABAN ZAN MIN MMATARIN AW KUNTUM MARZAA AN TAZAU’OOA AASLEHATAKUM WA KHOZOO HEZRAKUM INNAL LAAHA A-A’DDA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\nWhen thou (O Messenger) art with them, and standest to lead them in prayer, Let one party of them stand up (in prayer) with thee, Taking their arms with them: When they finish their prostrations, let them Take their position in the rear. And let the other party come up which hath not yet prayed - and let them pray with thee, Taking all precaution, and bearing arms: the Unbelievers wish, if ye were negligent of your arms and your baggage, to assault you in a single rush. But there is no blame on you if ye put away your arms because of the inconvenience of rain or because ye are ill; but take (every) precaution for yourselves. For the Unbelievers Allah hath prepared a humiliating punishment. \nفَاِذَا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ قِيَامًا وَّقُعُوْدًا وَّعَلٰى جُنُوْبِكُمْ ۚؕ فَاِذَا اطْمَاْنَنْتُمْ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ۚ اِنَّ الصَّلٰوةَ كَانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ كِتٰبًا مَّوْقُوْتًا‏(103)\nFA-EZAA QAZAYTUMU SALAATA FAZKORUL LAAHA QEEAMAN WWAQUU’OODAN WWAA’ALAA JUNOOBEKUM FA-EZAA ATMAANANTUM FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA INNAL SALAATA KAANAT A’LAL MOAMENEEN KETAABAA MMAWQOOTAN.\nWhen ye pass (Congregational) prayers, celebrate Allah's praises, standing, sitting down, or lying down on your sides; but when ye are free from danger, set up Regular Prayers: For such prayers are enjoined on believers at stated times. \nوَلَا تَهِنُوْا فِى ابْتِغَآءِ الْقَوْمِ ؕ اِنْ تَكُوْنُوْا تَاْلَمُوْنَ فَاِنَّهُمْ يَاْلَمُوْنَ كَمَا تَاْلَمُوْنَ ۚ وَتَرْجُوْنَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ ؕ وَ كَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(104)\nWA LAA TAHENOOA FIL ABTEGHAAE QAWMIL IN TAKOONOO TAALAMOONA FA INNAHUM YAALAMOONA KAMAA TAALAMOONA WATARJOONA MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA YARJOON WA KAANA LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAnd slacken not in following up the enemy: If ye are suffering hardships, they are suffering similar hardships; but ye have Hope from Allah, while they have none. And Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom. \nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ لِتَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ بِمَاۤ اَرٰٮكَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَلَا تَكُنْ لِّلْخَآئِنِيْنَ خَصِيْمًا ۙ‏(105)\nINNAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KETAABA BIL-HAQQE LETAHKUMA BAYNA NAASE BEMAA AARAAKA LAAHO WA LAA TAKUN LLELKHAAENEENA KHASEEMAN.\nWe have sent down to thee the Book in truth, that thou mightest judge between men, as guided by Allah: so be not (used) as an advocate by those who betray their trust; \nوَّاسْتَغْفِرِ اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا ۚ‏(106)\nWWAASTAGHFERE LAAHA INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nBut seek the forgiveness of Allah; for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَلَا تُجَادِلْ عَنِ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْتَانُوْنَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ مَنْ كَانَ خَوَّانًا اَثِيْمًا ۙ ۚ‏(107)\nWA LAA TUJAADEL A’NIL LAZEENA YAKHTAANOONA ANFOSAHUM INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MAN KAANA KHAWANAN AASEEMAN.\nContend not on behalf of such as betray their own souls; for Allah loveth not one given to perfidy and crime: \nيَّسْتَخْفُوْنَ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يَسْتَخْفُوْنَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ وَهُوَ مَعَهُمْ اِذْ يُبَيِّتُوْنَ مَا لَا يَرْضٰى مِنَ الْقَوْلِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطًا‏(108)\nYYASTAKHFOONA MENAL NAASE WA LAA YASTAKHFOONA MENAL LAAHE WA HOWA MA-A’HUM IZ YUBAYTOONA MAA LAA YARZAA MENAL AL-QAWLE KAANAL LAAHO BEMAA YA’MALOON MUHEETAN.\nThey may hide (Their crimes) from men, but they cannot hide (Them) from Allah, seeing that He is in their midst when they plot by night, in words that He cannot approve: And Allah Doth compass round all that they do. \nهٰۤاَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ جَادَلْتُمْ عَنْهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا فَمَنْ يُّجَادِلُ اللّٰهَ عَنْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَمْ مَّنْ يَّكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيْلًا‏(109)\nHAANTUM HAAOOLAAA-E JAADALTUM A’NHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA FAMAN YYUJAADELU LAAHA A’NHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE AM MAN YYAKOONU A’LAYHIM WAKEELAA.\nAh! These are the sort of men on whose behalf ye may contend in this world; but who will contend with Allah on their behalf on the Day of Judgment, or who will carry their affairs through? \nوَ مَنْ يَّعْمَلْ سُوْٓءًا اَوْ يَظْلِمْ نَفْسَهٗ ثُمَّ يَسْتَغْفِرِ اللّٰهَ يَجِدِ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(110)\nWA MAN YA’MAL SOOO-AN AW YAZLEM NAFSAH SUMMA YASTAGHFERE LAAHA YAJEDE LAAHA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nIf any one does evil or wrongs his own soul but afterwards seeks Allah's forgiveness, he will find Allah Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَمَنْ يَّكْسِبْ اِثْمًا فَاِنَّمَا يَكْسِبُهٗ عَلٰى نَفْسِهٖؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(111)\nWA MAN YYAKSEB ISMAN FA-INNAMAA YAKSEBUH A’LAA NAFSEH KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nAnd if any one earns sin. he earns it against His own soul: for Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom. \nوَمَنْ يَّكْسِبْ خَطِيْٓئَةً اَوْ اِثْمًا ثُمَّ يَرْمِ بِهٖ بَرِيْٓئًا فَقَدِ احْتَمَلَ بُهْتَانًا وَّاِثْمًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(112)\nWA MAN YYAKSEB KHATEEATAN AW ISMAN SUMMA YARME BEHI BAREEAN FAQADEH AHTAMALA BOHTAANANW WA ISMAM MOBEENAA.\nBut if any one earns a fault or a sin and throws it on to one that is innocent, He carries (on himself) (Both) a falsehood and a flagrant sin. \nوَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ لَهَمَّتْ طَّآئِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ يُّضِلُّوْكَ ؕ وَمَا يُضِلُّوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَضُرُّوْنَكَ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ وَاَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَكَ مَا لَمْ تَكُنْ تَعْلَمُؕ وَكَانَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ عَظِيْمًا‏(113)\nWA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKA WA RAHMATOHU LAHAMMAT TAAA-EFATUM MINHUM AN YYUZELLOOKA WA MAA YUZELLOONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YAZURROONAKA MIN SHAY-IN WA ANZALA LAAHO A’LAYKA KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WAA’ALLAMAKA MAA LAM TAKUN TAA’LAMU KAANAL FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKA A’ZEEMAA.\nBut for the Grace of Allah to thee and his Mercy, a party of them would certainly have plotted to lead thee astray. But (in fact) they will only Lead their own souls astray, and to thee they can do no harm in the least. For Allah hath sent down to thee the Book and wisdom and taught thee what thou Knewest not (before): And great is the Grace of Allah unto thee. \nلَا خَيْرَ فِىْ كَثِيْرٍ مِّنْ نَّجْوٰٮهُمْ اِلَّا مَنْ اَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ اَوْ مَعْرُوْفٍ اَوْ اِصْلَاحٍۢ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ ؕ وَمَن يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ ابْتِغَآءَ مَرْضَاتِ اللّٰهِ فَسَوْفَ نُؤْتِيْهِ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(114)\nLAA KHAYRAZ FEE KASEERIM MIN NNAJWAAHUM ILLAA MAN AMARAL BE-SADAQATIN AW MAA’ROOFIN AW AESLAAHIN BAYNA NAASE WAMAN MAN-Y ZAA LEKA TEGHAAA-A MARZAATIL LAAHE FA-SAWFA NUTEEHE AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\n In most of their secret talks there is no good: But if one exhorts to a deed of charity or justice or conciliation between men, (Secrecy is permissible): To him who does this, seeking the good pleasure of Allah, We shall soon give a reward of the highest (value). \nوَمَنْ يُّشَاقِقِ الرَّسُوْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدٰى وَ يَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيْلِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ نُوَلِّهٖ مَا تَوَلّٰى وَنُصْلِهٖ جَهَنَّمَ ؕ وَسَآءَتْ مَصِيْرًا‏(115)\nWA MAN YYUSHAAQEQE YATTABE-U’R MIN BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHUL HODAA WA YATTABEA’ GHAYRA SABEELIL MOAMENEEN NOOLLEH MAA TAWALLAA WANUSLEH JAHANNAMA WA SAA-AT MASEERAA.\nIf anyone contends with the Messenger even after guidance has been plainly conveyed to him, and follows a path other than that becoming to men of Faith, We shall leave him in the path he has chosen, and land him in Hell, what an evil refuge! \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ اَنْ يُّشْرَكَ بِهٖ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(116)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAGHFERO AN YYUSHRAKA BEHI WA YAGHFERO MAA DOONA ZAA LEKA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAQAD ZALLA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nAllah forgiveth not (The sin of) joining other gods with Him; but He forgiveth whom He pleaseth other sins than this: one who joins other gods with Allah, Hath strayed far, far away (from the right). \nاِنْ يَّدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اِنٰثًا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّدْعُوْنَ اِلَّا شَيْطٰنًا مَّرِيْدًا ۙ‏(117)\nIN YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI ILLAA AENAASAN WA YAD-O’ONA ILLAA SHAYTAANAN MMAREEDAN.\n(The Pagans), leaving Him, call but upon female deities: They call but upon satan the persistent rebel! \nلَّعَنَهُ اللّٰهُ ۘ وَقَالَ لَاَ تَّخِذَنَّ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ نَصِيْبًا مَّفْرُوْضًا ۙ‏(118)\nLLAA’ANAHU LAAHO WA QAALA LAA TTAKHEZANNA MIN E’BAADEKAS NASEEBAN MMAFROOZAN.\nAllah did curse him, but he said: “I will take of Thy servants a portion Marked off; \nوَّلَاُضِلَّنَّهُمْ وَلَاُمَنِّيَنَّهُمْ وَلَاٰمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُبَتِّكُنَّ اٰذَانَ الْاَنْعَامِ وَلَاٰمُرَنَّهُمْ فَلَيُغَيِّرُنَّ خَلْقَ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَّخِذِ الشَّيْطٰنَ وَلِيًّا مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَقَدْ خَسِرَ خُسْرَانًا مُّبِيْنًا ؕ‏(119)\nWWALAAZELLANNAHUM WALAAMANNEENNAHUM WALAAMURANNAHUM FALAYUBATTEKUNNA AAAZAANA AL-AANA’AAME WALAAMURANNAHUM FALAYUGHAYRUNNA KHALQA LAAH WA MAN YYATTAKHEZE ASH-SHAYTAANA WALIYYANW MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAQAD KHASERA KHUSRAANAN MOBEENAA.\n“I will mislead them, and I will create in them false desires; I will order them to slit the ears of cattle, and to deface the (fair) nature created by Allah.” Whoever, forsaking Allah, takes satan for a friend, hath of a surety suffered a loss that is manifest. \nيَعِدُهُمْ وَيُمَنِّيْهِمْ ؕ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(120)\nYAE’EDUHUM WAYUMANNEEHEM WA MAA YAE’EDUHUMU SHAYTAANO ILLAA GHOROORAA.\nSatan makes them promises, and creates in them false desires; but satan's promises are nothing but deception. \nاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ وَلَا يَجِدُوْنَ عَنْهَا مَحِيْصًا‏(121)\nOOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL WA LAA YAJEDOONA A’NHAA MAHEESAN.\nThey (his dupes) will have their dwelling in Hell, and from it they will find no way of escape. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَنُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا ؕ وَمَنْ اَصْدَقُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ قِيْلًا‏(122)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SANUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQAN WA MAN AASDAQU MENAL LAAHE QEELAN.\nBut those who believe and do deeds of righteousness, we shall soon admit them to gardens, with rivers flowing beneath, to dwell therein for ever. Allah's promise is the truth, and whose word can be truer than Allah's? \nلَيْسَ بِاَمَانِيِّكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَمَانِىِّ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِؕ مَنْ يَّعْمَلْ سُوْٓءًا يُّجْزَ بِهٖۙ وَ لَا يَجِدْ لَهٗ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا‏(123)\nLAYSA BEAAMAANEEKUM WA LAA AAMAANEAAAE AHLIL AL-KETAABE MAN YA’MAL SOOO-AN YYUJZA BEHI WA LAA YAJID LAHU MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\nNot your desires, nor those of the People of the Book (can prevail): whoever works evil, will be requited accordingly. Nor will he find, besides Allah, any protector or helper. \nوَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ مِنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ نَقِيْرًا‏(124)\nWA MAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON NAQEERAN.\nIf any do deeds of righteousness, be they male or female - and have faith, they will enter Heaven, and not the least injustice will be done to them. \nوَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ دِيْنًا مِّمَّنْ اَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهٗ لِلّٰهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ وَّاتَّبَعَ مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا ؕ وَاتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ خَلِيْلًا‏(125)\nWA MAN AHSANO DEENAN MIMMAYN ASLAMA WAJHAHU LILLAAHE WA HOWA MOHSENUN WWAATTABAA’A MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA TAKHAZA LAAHO IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELAN.\nWho can be better in religion than one who submits his whole self to Allah, does good, and follows the way of Abraham the true in Faith? For Allah did take Abraham for a friend. \nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ مُّحِيْطًا‏(126)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAANAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN MMUHEETAN.\nBut to Allah belong all things in the heavens and on earth: And He it is that Encompasseth all things. \nوَيَسْتَفْتُوْنَكَ فِى النِّسَآءِ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يُفْتِيْكُمْ فِيْهِنَّ ۙ وَمَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ فِىْ يَتٰمَى النِّسَآءِ الّٰتِىْ لَا تُؤْتُوْنَهُنَّ مَا كُتِبَ لَهُنَّ وَتَرْغَبُوْنَ اَنْ تَنْكِحُوْهُنَّ وَالْمُسْتَضْعَفِيْنَ مِنَ الْوِلْدَانِ ۙ وَاَنْ تَقُوْمُوْا لِلْيَتٰمٰى بِالْقِسْطِ ؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِهٖ عَلِيْمًا‏(127)\nWAYASTAFTOONAKA FIL NESAAA-E QOLIL LAAHO YUFTEEKUM FEEHINNA WA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM FIL KETAABE FEE YATAAMAA NESAAA-E KHAALEKA LAA TUTOONAHUNNA MAA KOTEBA LAHUNNA WATARGHABOONA AN TANKEHOOHUNNA WAL MUSTAZA’AFEENA MENAL AL-WELDAANE WA TAQOOMOOA LIL-YATAAMAA BIL QISTE WA MAA TAF-A’LOO MIN KHAYRIN FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEHI A’LEEMAN.\nThey ask thy instruction concerning the women say: Allah doth instruct you about them: And (remember) what hath been rehearsed unto you in the Book, concerning the orphans of women to whom ye give not the portions prescribed, and yet whom ye desire to marry, as also concerning the children who are weak and oppressed: that ye stand firm for justice to orphans. There is not a good deed which ye do, but Allah is well-acquainted therewith. \nوَاِنِ امْرَاَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْۢ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوْزًا اَوْ اِعْرَاضًا فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَاۤ اَنْ يُّصْلِحَا بَيْنَهُمَا صُلْحًا ؕ وَالصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ ؕ وَاُحْضِرَتِ الْاَنْفُسُ الشُّحَّ ؕ وَاِنْ تُحْسِنُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(128)\nWA ENIS AMRAATUN KHAAFAT MIN BAA’LEHAA NUSHOOZAN AW AEA’RAAZAN FALAA JONAAHA FEEMAF AN YYUSLEHAA BAYNAHOMAA SULHAN WAALSSULHU KHAYRUL WAAHZERATE AL-AANFUSU ASH-SHUHHA WA TUHSENOOA WA TATTAQOO FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\nIf a wife fears cruelty or desertion on her husband's part, there is no blame on them if they arrange an amicable settlement between themselves; and such settlement is best; even though men's souls are swayed by greed. But if ye do good and practise self-restraint, Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do. \nوَلَنْ تَسْتَطِيْعُوْۤا اَنْ تَعْدِلُوْا بَيْنَ النِّسَآءِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتُمْ فَلَا تَمِيْلُوْا كُلَّ الْمَيْلِ فَتَذَرُوْهَا كَالْمُعَلَّقَةِ ؕ وَاِنْ تُصْلِحُوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(129)\nWA LAN TASTATEEU’OOA AN TAA’DELOOA BAYNA NESAAA-E WA LAW HARASTUM FALAA TAMEELOOA KULLA AL-MAYLE FATAZAROOHAA KAALMUA’ALLAQATE WA TUSLEHOOA WA TATTAQOO FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nYe are never able to be fair and just as between women, even if it is your ardent desire: But turn not away (from a woman) altogether, so as to leave her (as it were) hanging (in the air). If ye come to a friendly understanding, and practise self-restraint, Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَاِنْ يَّتَفَرَّقَا يُغْنِ اللّٰهُ كُلًّا مِّنْ سَعَتِهٖ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ وَاسِعًا حَكِيْمًا‏(130)\nWA YYATAFARRAQAA YUGHNE LAAHO KULLAN MIN SAA’ATEH KAANAL LAAHO WAASEA’AN HAKEEMAA.\nBut if they disagree (and must part), Allah will provide abundance for all from His all-reaching bounty: for Allah is He that careth for all and is Wise. \nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ وَلَقَدْ وَصَّيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَاِيَّاكُمْ اَنِ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ وَاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَنِيًّا حَمِيْدًا‏(131)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA LAQAD WASSAYNAA LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA MIN QABLEKUM WA IYYAAKUM SAALEHAN TAQUL LAAHA WA TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAANAL LAAHO GHANEEA HAMEEDAN.\nTo Allah belong all things in the heavens and on earth. Verily we have directed the People of the Book before you, and you (o Muslims) to fear Allah. But if ye deny Him, lo! unto Allah belong all things in the heavens and on earth, and Allah is free of all wants, worthy of all praise. \nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(132)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nYea, unto Allah belong all things in the heavens and on earth, and enough is Allah to carry through all affairs. \nاِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ اَيُّهَا النَّاسُ وَيَاْتِ بِاٰخَرِيْنَؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ قَدِيْرًا‏(133)\nIN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM AYYOHAL NAASO WA TAKOONOO BEAAAKHAREENA KAANAL LAAHO A’LAA ZAALEKA QADEERAA.\nIf it were His will, He could destroy you, o mankind, and create another race; for He hath power this to do. \nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ ثَوَابَ الدُّنْيَا فَعِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ثَوَابُ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ سَمِيْعًاۢ بَصِيْرًا‏(134)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO SAWAABA DUNYAA FA I’NDAL LAAHE SAWAABUL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH KAANAL LAAHO SAMEE-A’M BASEERAA.\nIf any one desires a reward in this life, in Allah's (gift) is the reward (both) of this life and of the hereafter: for Allah is He that heareth and seeth (all things). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُوْنُوْا قَوَّامِيْنَ بِالْقِسْطِ شُهَدَآءَ لِلّٰهِ وَلَوْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَوِ الْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْاَقْرَبِيْنَ ؕ اِنْ يَّكُنْ غَنِيًّا اَوْ فَقِيْرًا فَاللّٰهُ اَوْلٰى بِهِمَا فَلَا تَتَّبِعُوا الْهَوٰٓى اَنْ تَعْدِلُوْا ۚ وَاِنْ تَلْوٗۤا اَوْ تُعْرِضُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرًا‏(135)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOONOO QAWAMEENA BIL QISTE SHOHADAAA-A LILLAAHE WA LAW A’LAA ANFOSEKUM AWE’ AL-WAALEDAYNE WAL AQRABEENA IN YYAKUN GHANEEA AW FAQEERAN FAL-LAAHO AAWLAA BEHEMAA FALAA TATTABEU’OOA AL-HAWAA AN TAA’DELOOA WA TALWA AW TUA’REZOOA FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERAA.\n O ye who believe! stand out firmly for justice, as witnesses to Allah, even as against yourselves, or your parents, or your kin, and whether it be (against) rich or poor: for Allah can best protect both. Follow not the lusts (of your hearts), lest ye swerve, and if ye distort (justice) or decline to do justice, verily Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَالْكِتٰبِ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِهٖ وَالْكِتٰبِ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَلٰٓئِكَتِهٖ وَكُتُبِهٖ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(136)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WAL KETAABE LAZEE NAZZALAL A’LAA RASOOLEHI WAL KETAABE LAZEE ANZALAL MIN QABL WA WA MAN YAKFUR BIL-LAAHE WA MALAA-EKATEHI WA KOTOBEHI WA ROSOLEHI WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE FAQAD ZALLA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nO ye who believe! Believe in Allah and His Messenger, and the scripture which He hath sent to His Messenger and the scripture which He sent to those before (him). Any who denieth Allah, His angels, His Books, His Messengers, and the Day of Judgment, hath gone far, far astray. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ اٰمَنُوْا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوْا ثُمَّ ازْدَادُوْا كُفْرًا لَّمْ يَكُنِ اللّٰهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلَا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ سَبِيْلًا ؕ‏(137)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO SUMMA KAFAROO SUMMA AAMANOO SUMMA KAFAROO SUMMA AZDAADOOA KUFRAN LAM YAKONIL LAAHO LEEGHFERA LAHUM WA LAA LEEHDEEHUM SABEELAA.\nThose who believe, then reject faith, then believe (again) and (again) reject faith, and go on increasing in unbelief, Allah will not forgive them nor guide them nor guide them on the way. \nبَشِّرِ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ بِاَنَّ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًاۙ‏(138)\nBASH-SHERIL MONAAFEQEENA BE-ANNAL LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nTo the Hypocrites give the glad tidings that there is for them (but) a grievous penalty;- \nۨالَّذِيْنَ يَتَّخِذُوْنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ اَيَبْتَغُوْنَ عِنْدَهُمُ الْعِزَّةَ فَاِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ‏(139)\nLAZEENA YATTAKHEZOONA KAAFEREEN AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL MOAMENEEN AAYABTAGHOONA E’ENDAHUMU AL-E’EZZATA FA-INNAL AL-E’EZZATA LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A.\nYea, to those who take for friends unbelievers rather than believers: is it honour they seek among them? Nay, all honour is with Allah. \nوَقَدْ نَزَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ اِذَا سَمِعْتُمْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يُكْفَرُ بِهَا وَيُسْتَهْزَاُبِهَا فَلَا تَقْعُدُوْا مَعَهُمْ حَتّٰى يَخُوْضُوْا فِىْ حَدِيْثٍ غَيْرِهٖۤ  ۖ اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا مِّثْلُهُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ جَامِعُالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَالْكٰفِرِيْنَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ جَمِيْعَاۨ ۙ‏(140)\nWA QAD NAZZALAL A’LAYKUM FIL KETAABE AN EZAA SAMEA’TUM AAYAATIL LAAHE YUKFARU BEHAA WAYUSTAHZAABEHAA FALAA TAQU’UDOOA MA-A’HUM HATTAA YAKHOOZOOA FEE HADEESIN GHAYREH INNAKUM EZAL MMESLUHUM INNAL LAAHA JAAMEU’UALMUNAAFEQEENA WA KAAFEREEN FEE JAHANNAMA JAMEEA’AA.\nAlready has He sent you Word in the Book, that when ye hear the signs of Allah held in defiance and ridicule, ye are not to sit with them unless they turn to a different theme: if ye did, ye would be like them. For Allah will collect the hypocrites and those who defy faith - all in Hell:- \nالَّذِيْنَ يَتَرَ بَّصُوْنَ بِكُمْ ۚ فَاِنْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فَتْحٌ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ نَكُنْ مَّعَكُمْ  ۖ وَاِنْ كَانَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ نَصِيْبٌۙ قَالُوْۤا اَلَمْ نَسْتَحْوِذْ عَلَيْكُمْ وَنَمْنَعْكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ فَاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَلَنْ يَّجْعَلَ اللّٰهُ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ سَبِيْلًا‏(141)\nLAZEENA MOTALLAQAATO BBASOONA BEKUM FA-IN KAANA LAKUM FATHUN MENAL LAAHE QAALOO ALAM NAKUN MMAA’AKUM WA KAANA LIL KAAFEREENA NASEEBUM QAALOO ALAM NASTAHWEZ A’LAYKUM WANAMNAA’KUM MENAL MOAMENEEN FAL-LAAHO YAHKOMO BAYNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA LAN YYAJA’ALA LAAHO LIL KAAFEREENA A’LAL MOAMENEEN SABEELAA.\n(These are) the ones who wait and watch about you: if ye do gain a victory from Allah, they say: “Were we not with you?”- but if the unbelievers gain a success, they say (to them): “Did we not gain an advantage over you, and did we not guard you from the believers?” but Allah will judge betwixt you on the Day of Judgment. And never will Allah grant to the unbelievers a way (to triumphs) over the believers. \nاِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ يُخٰدِعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَهُوَ خَادِعُوْهُمْ ۚ وَاِذَا قَامُوْۤا اِلَى الصَّلٰوةِ قَامُوْا كُسَالٰى ۙ يُرَآءُوْنَ النَّاسَ وَلَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اللّٰهَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(142)\nINNAL MONAAFEQEENA YOKHAADE-O’ONAL LAAHA WA HOWA KHAADEU’OOHUM WA EZAA QAAMOOA ELAL AS-SALAAWTE QAAMOOA KUSAALAA YORAAA-OONA NAASA WA LAA YAZKUROONA LAAHA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nThe Hypocrites - they think they are over-reaching Allah, but He will over-reach them: When they stand up to prayer, they stand without earnestness, to be seen of men, but little do they hold Allah in remembrance; \nمُّذَبْذَبِيْنَ بَيْنَ  ۖ ذٰ لِكَ لَاۤ اِلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰى هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهٗ سَبِيْلًا‏(143)\nMMUZABZABEENA BAYNA ZAA LEKA LAA ELAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA LAA ELAA HAAOOLAAA-E WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FALAN TAJEDA LAHU SABEELAA.\n(They are) distracted in mind even in the midst of it, being (sincerely) for neither one group nor for another whom Allah leaves straying, never wilt thou find for him the way. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ اَ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَجْعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(144)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTAKHEZOOA KAAFEREEN AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL MOAMENEEN A’ZAABAN TOREEDOONA AN TAJ-A’LOO LILLAAHE A’LAYKUM SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nO ye who believe! Take not for friends unbelievers rather than believers: Do ye wish to offer Allah an open proof against yourselves? \nاِنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ فِى الدَّرْكِ الْاَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ ۚ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيْرًا ۙ‏(145)\nINNAL MONAAFEQEENA FIL AD-DARKE AL-AASFALE MENAL NAAR WA LAN TAJEDA LAHUM NASEERAA.\nThe Hypocrites will be in the lowest depths of the Fire: no helper wilt thou find for them;- \nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاَصْلَحُوْا وَاعْتَصَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاَخْلَصُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لِلّٰهِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَعَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يُؤْتِ اللّٰهُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(146)\nILLAA LAZEENA TAABOO WA ASLAHOO WAAA’TASAMOOA BIL-LAAHE WAAKHLASOOA DEENAHUM LILLAAHE FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAAHA MOAMENEEN WA SAWFA YUTE LAAHO MOAMENEEN AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nExcept for those who repent, mend (their lives) hold fast to Allah, and purify their religion as in Allah's sight: if so they will be (numbered) with the believers. And soon will Allah grant to the believers a reward of immense value. \nمَا يَفْعَلُ اللّٰهُ بِعَذَابِكُمْ اِنْ شَكَرْتُمْ وَاٰمَنْتُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ شَاكِرًا عَلِيْمًا‏(147)\nMAA YAF-A’LO LAAHO BEA’AZAABEKUM IN SHAKARTUM WA AAMANTUM KAANAL LAAHO SHAAKERAWN A’LEEMAN.\nWhat can Allah gain by your punishment, if ye are grateful and ye believe? Nay, it is Allah that recogniseth (all good), and knoweth all things. \nلَا يُحِبُّ اللّٰهُ الْجَهْرَ بِالسُّوْٓءِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ اِلَّا مَنْ ظُلِمَؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ سَمِيْعًا عَلِيْمًا‏(148)\nLAA YOHIBBUL LAAHO JAHRA BIS-SOOO-E MENAL AL-QAWLE ILLAA MAN ZULEMA KAANAL LAAHO SAMEE-A’M A’LEEMAN.\nAllah loveth not that evil should be noised abroad in public speech, except where injustice hath been done; for Allah is He who heareth and knoweth all things. \nاِنْ تُبْدُوْا خَيْرًا اَوْ تُخْفُوْهُ اَوْ تَعْفُوْا عَنْ سُوْٓءٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ عَفُوًّا قَدِيْرًا‏(149)\nIN IN TUBDOO KHAYRAN AW TUKHFOOHO AW TAA’FOOA A’N SOOO-IN FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA A’AFOOA QADEERAA.\nWhether ye publish a good deed or conceal it or cover evil with pardon, verily Allah doth blot out (sins) and hath power (in the judgment of values). \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يُّفَرِّقُوْا بَيْنَ اللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ نُؤْمِنُ بِبَعْضٍ وَّنَكْفُرُ بِبَعْضٍۙ وَّيُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ سَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(150)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKFOROON BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA YOREEDOONA AN YYUFARREQOOA BAYNA LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA YAQOOLOONA NOAMENO BE-BA’Z WWANAKFURU BE-BA’Z WWAYUREEDOONA AN YYATTAKHEZOOA BAYNA ZAA LEKA SABEELAA.\nThose who deny Allah and His messengers, and (those who) wish to separate Allah from His messengers, saying: “We believe in some but reject others”: And (those who) wish to take a course midway, \nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ حَقًّا ۚ وَ اَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابًا مُّهِيْنًا‏(151)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAAFEROON HAQQAN WA A-A’TADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABAN MOHEENAA.\nThey are in truth (equally) unbelievers; and we have prepared for unbelievers a humiliating punishment. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ وَلَمْ يُفَرِّقُوْا بَيْنَ اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ اُولٰٓئِكَ سَوْفَ يُؤْتِيْهِمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(152)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA LAM YUFARREQOOA BAYNA AHADIM MINHUM OOLAAA-EKA SAWFA YUTEEHEM AUJOORAHUM KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nTo those who believe in Allah and His messengers and make no distinction between any of the messengers, we shall soon give their (due) rewards: for Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nيَسْئَلُكَ اَهْلُ الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْهِمْ كِتٰبًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فَقَدْ سَاَ لُوْا مُوْسٰٓى اَكْبَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ فَقَالُوْۤا اَرِنَا اللّٰهَ جَهْرَةً فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ بِظُلْمِهِمْ ۚ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُ فَعَفَوْنَا عَنْ ذٰ لِكَ ۚ وَاٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى سُلْطٰنًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(153)\nYAS-ALOKAN AAHLU KETAABE AN TUNAZZELA A’LAYHIM KETAABAA MENAL SAMAAA-E FAQAD HAQ LOOA MOOSAA AAKBARA MIN ZAA LEKA FA-QAALOO ARENAL LAAHA JAHRATN FA-AKHAZATHOMUR SAA-E’QATO BEZULMEHEM SUMMA ATTAKHAZOOA I’JLA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-ATHOMUL BAYYENAATO FA A’FAWNAA A’N ZAA LEKA WA AATAYNAA MOOSAA SULTAANAN MOBEENAA.\nThe people of the Book ask thee to cause a book to descend to them from heaven: Indeed they asked Moses for an even greater (miracle), for they said: “Show us Allah in public,” but they were dazed for their presumption, with thunder and lightning. Yet they worshipped the calf even after clear signs had come to them; even so we forgave them; and gave Moses manifest proofs of authority. \nوَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَهُمُ الطُّوْرَ بِمِيْثَاقِهِمْ وَقُلْنَا لَهُمُ ادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا وَّقُلْنَا لَهُمْ لَا تَعْدُوْا فِى السَّبْتِ وَاَخَذْنَا مِنْهُمْ مِّيْثَاقًا غَلِيْظًا‏(154)\nWA RAFA’NAA FAWQAHUMU FAWQAKOMUT BEMEESAAQEHEM WA LAHOMUL ADKHULOOA BAABA SUJJADANW WWAQULNAA LAHUM LAA TAA’DOOA FIL SABTE AKHAZNAA MINHUM MMEESAAQAN GHALEEZAA.\nAnd for their covenant we raised over them (the towering height) of Mount (Sinai); and (on another occasion) we said: “Enter the gate with humility”; and (once again) we commanded them: “Transgress not in the matter of the sabbath.” And we took from them a solemn covenant. \nفَبِمَا نَقْضِهِمْ مِّيْثَاقَهُمْ وَكُفْرِهِمْ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَقَتْلِهِمُ الْاَنْۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَّقَوْلِهِمْ قُلُوْبُنَا غُلْفٌ ؕ بَلْ طَبَعَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهَا بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(155)\nFA BEMAA NAQZEHEM MMEESAAQAHUM WAKUFREHEM BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WAQATLEHEMU AL-AANBEEAAAA BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN WWAQAWLEHEM QOLOOBONAA GHULFUN BAL TABAA’A LAAHO A’LAYHAA BEKUFREHIM FALAA YOAMENOONA ILLAA QALEELAA.\n(They have incurred divine displeasure): In that they broke their covenant; that they rejected the signs of Allah; that they slew the Messengers in defiance of right; that they said, “Our hearts are the wrappings (which preserve Allah's Word; We need no more)”;- Nay, Allah hath set the seal on their hearts for their blasphemy, and little is it they believe;- \nوَّبِكُفْرِهِمْ وَقَوْلِهِمْ عَلٰى مَرْيَمَ بُهْتَانًا عَظِيْمًا ۙ‏(156)\nWWABEKUFREHEM WA QAWLEHIM A’LAA MARYAMAL BOHTAANANW A’ZEEMAA.\nThat they rejected Faith; that they uttered against Mary a grave false charge; \nوَّقَوْلِهِمْ اِنَّا قَتَلْنَا الْمَسِيْحَ عِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوْهُ وَمَا صَلَبُوْهُ وَلٰكِنْ شُبِّهَ لَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ ؕ مَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ اِلَّا اتِّبَاعَ الظَّنِّ ۚ وَمَا قَتَلُوْهُ يَقِيْنًا ۢ ۙ‏(157)\nWWAQAWLEHEM INNAA QATALNAA AL-MASEEHA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL TOAZOO LAAHE WA MAA QATALOOHU WA MAA SALABOOHU WA LAAKIL SHUBBEHA LAHUM WA INNA LAZEENA TALAFOO FEEHE LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MAA LAHUM BEHI MIN I’LMIN ILLAA ATTEBAAA’A AZ-ZANNE WA MAA QATALOOHU YAQEENAN.\nThat they said (in boast), “We killed Christ Jesus the son of Mary, the Messenger of Allah”;- but they killed him not, nor crucified him, but so it was made to appear to them, and those who differ therein are full of doubts, with no (certain) knowledge, but only conjecture to follow, for of a surety they killed him not:- \nبَلْ رَّفَعَهُ اللّٰهُ اِلَيْهِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(158)\nBAL RRAFAA’AHU LAAHO ELAYHE KAANAL LAAHO A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\nNay, Allah raised him up unto Himself; and Allah is Exalted in Power, Wise;- \nوَاِنْ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ اِلَّا لَيُؤْمِنَنَّ بِهٖ قَبْلَ مَوْتِهٖ ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيْدًا ۚ‏(159)\nWA MIN AHLIL KETAABE ILLAA LAYUMENANNA BEHI QABLA MAWTEH WA YAWMA QEYAAMATE LAHUL A’LAYHIM SHAHEEDAA.\nAnd there is none of the People of the Book but must believe in him before his death; and on the Day of Judgment he will be a witness against them;- \nفَبِظُلْمٍ مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ طَيِّبٰتٍ اُحِلَّتْ لَهُمْ وَبِصَدِّهِمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ كَثِيْرًا ۙ‏(160)\nFABEZULMIN MENAL LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIM TAYBAATIN AUHELLAT LAHUM WABESADDEHEM A’N SABEELIL LAAHE KASEERAA.\nFor the iniquity of the Jews We made unlawful for them certain (foods) good and wholesome which had been lawful for them;- in that they hindered many from Allah's Way;- \nوَّاَخْذِهِمُ الرِّبٰوا وَقَدْ نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَاَكْلِهِمْ اَمْوَالَ النَّاسِ بِالْبَاطِلِ ؕ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مِنْهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا‏(161)\nWWAAKHZEHEMU REBAA WA QAD NUHOOA A’NHO WAAKLEHEM AAMWAALA NAASE BIL-BAATELE WA A-ATADNAA LIL KAAFEREENA MINHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nThat they took usury, though they were forbidden; and that they devoured men's substance wrongfully;- we have prepared for those among them who reject faith a grievous punishment. \nلٰكِنِ الرّٰسِخُوْنَ فِى الْعِلْمِ مِنْهُمْ وَالْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ وَالْمُقِيْمِيْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَالْمُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ سَنُؤْتِيْهِمْ اَجْرًا عَظِيْمًا‏(162)\nLAAKENE AR-RAASEKHOONA FIL I’LME MINHUM WAL MO’MENOONA YOAMENOONA BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLEKA WAL MUQEEMEENA SALAATA WAL MUTOONA ZAKAATA WA MOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE OOLAAA-EKA SANUTEEHEM AJRAN A’ZEEMAA.\nBut those among them who are well-grounded in knowledge, and the believers, believe in what hath been revealed to thee and what was revealed before thee: And (especially) those who establish regular prayer and practise regular charity and believe in Allah and in the Last Day: To them shall We soon give a great reward. \nاِنَّاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ كَمَاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى نُوْحٍ وَّالنَّبِيّٖنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ ۚ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَالْاَسْبَاطِ وَعِيْسٰى وَاَيُّوْبَ وَيُوْنُسَ وَهٰرُوْنَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ ۚ وَاٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ زَبُوْرًا ۚ‏(163)\nINNAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA KAMAA AAWHAYNAA ELAA NOOHIN WWAALNNABEENA MIN BA’DEHI WA AWHAYNAA ELAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WA ASBAATE WA E’ESAA WAAYYOOBA WAYOONUSA WA AALO WA SOLAYMAANA WA AATAYNAA DAAWOODA ZABOORAN.\n We have sent thee inspiration, as We sent it to Noah and the Messengers after him: we sent inspiration to Abraham, Isma'il, Isaac, Jacob and the Tribes, to Jesus, Job, Jonah, Aaron, and solomon, and to David We gave the Psalms. \nوَرُسُلًا قَدْ قَصَصْنٰهُمْ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَرُسُلًا لَّمْ نَقْصُصْهُمْ عَلَيْكَ ؕ وَكَلَّمَ اللّٰهُ مُوْسٰى تَكْلِيْمًا ۚ‏(164)\nWA ROSOLAN QAD QASASNAAHUM A’LAYKA MIN QABLO WA ROSOLAN LAM NAQSUSHUM A’LAYKA WA KALLAMAL LAAHO MOOSAA TAKLEEMAN.\nOf some messengers We have already told thee the story; of others We have not;- and to Moses Allah spoke direct;- \nرُسُلًا مُّبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَ لِئَلَّا يَكُوْنَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَى اللّٰهِ حُجَّةٌ ۢ بَعْدَ الرُّسُلِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَزِيْزًا حَكِيْمًا‏(165)\nROSOLAN MMUBASSHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN LE-ALLAA YAKOONA LIN-NAASE A’LAL LAAHE HUJJATUN BA’DA AR-RUSULE KAANAL LAAHO A’ZEEZAA HAKEEMAA.\nMessengers who gave good news as well as warning, that mankind, after (the coming) of the messengers, should have no plea against Allah: For Allah is Exalted in Power, Wise. \nلٰكِنِ اللّٰهُ يَشْهَدُ بِمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اِلَيْكَ اَنْزَلَهٗ بِعِلْمِهٖ ۚ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ يَشْهَدُوْنَ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًا ؕ‏(166)\nLAAKENE LAAHO YASHHADO BEMAA ANZALAL ELAYKA ELAYKUM BE-I’LMEHI WAL MALAAA-EKATO YASHHADOONA KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA.\nBut Allah beareth witness that what He hath sent unto thee He hath sent from His (own) knowledge, and the angels bear witness: But enough is Allah for a witness. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَ صَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا ضَلٰلًاۢ بَعِيْدًا‏(167)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA SADDOOA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE QAD ZALLOOA ZALAALAM BAE’EEDAN.\nThose who reject Faith and keep off (men) from the way of Allah, have verily strayed far, far away from the Path. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَظَلَمُوْا لَمْ يَكُنِ اللّٰهُ لِيَغْفِرَ لَهُمْ وَلَا لِيَهْدِيَهُمْ طَرِيْقًا ۙ‏(168)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA ZALAMOO LAM YAKONIL LAAHO LEEGHFERA LAHUM WA LAA LEEHDEEHUM TAREEQAN.\nThose who reject Faith and do wrong, Allah will not forgive them nor guide them to any way- \nاِلَّا طَرِيْقَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ وَكَانَ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرًا‏(169)\nILLAA TAREEQA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM KAANAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERAA.\nExcept the way of Hell, to dwell therein for ever. And this to Allah is easy. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الرَّسُوْلُ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاٰمِنُوْا خَيْرًا لَّكُمْ ؕ وَاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ عَلِيْمًا حَكِيْمًا‏(170)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAAKUMU RASOOLO BIL-HAQQE MIN RABBEKUM FA AAMENOO KHAYRAN LAKUM WA TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE KAANAL LAAHO A’LEEMAN HAKEEMAA.\nO Mankind! The Messenger hath come to you in truth from Allah: believe in him: It is best for you. But if ye reject Faith, to Allah belong all things in the heavens and on earth: And Allah is All-knowing, All-wise. \nيٰۤاَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا تَغْلُوْا فِىْ دِيْنِكُمْوَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ ؕ اِنَّمَا الْمَسِيْحُ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَكَلِمَتُهٗ ۚ اَ لْقٰٮهَاۤ اِلٰى مَرْيَمَ وَرُوْحٌ مِّنْهُ فَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرُسُلِهٖ ۚ وَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا ثَلٰثَةٌ ؕ اِنْتَهُوْا خَيْرًا لَّكُمْ ؕ اِنَّمَا اللّٰهُ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗۤ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ ۘ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ وَكِيْلًا‏(171)\nYAA AHLA KETAABE LAA TAGHLOOA FEE DEENEKUMWALAA TAQOOLOO A’LAL LAAHE ILLAA HAQQA INNAMAA AL-MASEEHU E’ESAB ABNU MARYAMAL RASOOLAL LAAHE WAKALEMATUH A’ZAABAN LQAAHAA ELAA MARYAMAL WAROOHUN MINHO FA AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WA ROSOLEHI WA LAA TAQOOLOO SALAASATUN AENTAHOOA KHAYRAN LAKUM INNAMAA LAAHO ELAAHUN WAAHED WALADAN AN YAKOONA LAHU WALADUN LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ KAFAA BIL-LAAHE WAKEELAA.\nO People of the Book! Commit no excesses in your religion: Nor say of Allah aught but the truth. Christ Jesus the son of Mary was (no more than) a messenger of Allah, and His Word, which He bestowed on Mary, and a spirit proceeding from Him: so believe in Allah and His messengers. Say not “Trinity” : desist: it will be better for you: for Allah is one Allah: Glory be to Him: (far exalted is He) above having a son. To Him belong all things in the heavens and on earth. And enough is Allah as a Disposer of affairs. \nلَنْ يَّسْتَنْكِفَ الْمَسِيْحُ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ عَبْدًا لِّلَّهِ وَلَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ وَمَنْ يَّسْتَنْكِفْ عَنْ عِبَادَ تِهٖ وَيَسْتَكْبِرْ فَسَيَحْشُرُهُمْ اِلَيْهِ جَمِيْعًا‏(172)\nLAN YYASTANKEFA AL-MASEEHU AN YAKOONA A’BDAN LILLAAH WA LAA TAHMELOHUL MOQARRABOON WA MAN YYASTANKEF A’N E’BAADAL TEH WAYASTAKBER FASAYAHSHURUHUM ELAYHE JAMEE-A’A.\nChrist disdaineth nor to serve and worship Allah, nor do the angels, those nearest (to Allah): those who disdain His worship and are arrogant, He will gather them all together unto Himself to (answer). \nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُوَفِّيْهِمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْ وَ يَزِيْدُهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖۚ وَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَنْكَفُوْا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا فَيُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا  ۙ وَّلَا يَجِدُوْنَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِيًّا وَّلَا نَصِيْرًا‏(173)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FAYOOFFEEHEM AUJOORAHUM WA YAZEEDUHUM MIN FAZLEHI WA AMMAA LAZEENA ASTANKAFOOA WAASTAKBAROOA FAYUA’AZZEBUHUM A’ZAABAN A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA WA LAA YAJEDOONA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYANW WA LAA NASEERAA.\nBut to those who believe and do deeds of righteousness, He will give their (due) rewards, and more, out of His bounty: But those who are disdainful and arrogant, He will punish with a grievous penalty; Nor will they find, besides Allah, any to protect or help them. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بُرْهَانٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَاَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ نُوْرًا مُّبِيْنًا‏(174)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAA-AKUM BURHAANUN MIN RABBEKUM WA ANZALNAA ELAYKUM NOORAN MOBEENAA.\nO mankind! verily there hath come to you a convincing proof from your Lord: For We have sent unto you a light (that is) manifest. \nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاعْتَصَمُوْا بِهٖ فَسَيُدْخِلُهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَةٍ مِّنْهُ وَفَضْلٍۙ وَّيَهْدِيْهِمْ اِلَيْهِ صِرَاطًا مُّسْتَقِيْمًا ؕ‏(175)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WAAA’TASAMOOA BEHI FASAYUDKHELUHUM FEE RAHMATIN MINHO WA FAZLIN WWAYAHDEEHEM ELAYHE SERAATAM MUSTAQEEMAA.\nThen those who believe in Allah, and hold fast to Him, soon will He admit them to mercy and grace from Himself, and guide them to Himself by a straight way. \nيَسْتَفْتُوْنَكَ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يُفْتِيْكُمْ فِى الْكَلٰلَةِ ؕ اِنِ امْرُؤٌا هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّلَهٗۤ اُخْتٌ فَلَهَا نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ ۚ وَهُوَ يَرِثُهَاۤ اِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ لَّهَا وَلَدٌ  ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَتَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَلَهُمَا الثُّلُثٰنِ مِمَّا تَرَكَ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانُوْۤا اِخْوَةً رِّجَالًا وَّنِسَآءً فَلِلذَّكَرِ مِثْلُ حَظِّ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اَنْ تَضِلُّوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(176)\nYASTAFTOONAKA QOLIL LAAHO YUFTEEKUM FIL AL-KALAALATE ENIS AMRUUNA HALAKA LAYSA LAHU WALADUN WWALAH AUKHTUN FA LAHAA NESFU MAA TARAKA WA HOWA YARESUHAA IN LAM YAKUL LLAHAA WALADUN FA-IN KAANATAA ASNATAYNE FA LAHOMAA AS-SULUSAANE MIMMAA TARAKA WA KAANOO AEKHWATAN RREJAALAN WWANESAAAN FALELZZAKARE LAZEE HAZZE AL-AUNSAYAYNE YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AN TAZELLOOA WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nThey ask thee for a legal decision. Say: Allah directs (thus) about those who leave no descendants or ascendants as heirs. If it is a man that dies, leaving a sister but no child, she shall have half the inheritance: If (such a deceased was) a woman, who left no child, Her brother takes her inheritance: If there are two sisters, they shall have two-thirds of the inheritance (between them): if there are brothers and sisters, (they share), the male having twice the share of the female. Thus doth Allah make clear to you (His law), lest ye err. And Allah hath knowledge of all things. ",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Madinah and has a total of 177 verses. In ‘Tafseer al-Burhan’ it is written that Imam Ali (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah on every Friday, he will remain safe from the squeezing in the grave (Fishaar-e-Qabr)."
